/* All 352 items from Brian Feeney's (Riot Games) "D&D Magic Items Megasheet", Core Set tab, in sheet order and quoted as written.
   n name, t type, r rarity (only Rare, Uncommon and Artifact are kept; the sheet's other entries in that column are working notes), u uses or charges, d description. */
window.FEENEY_ALL = [{"n": "Meteor Plate","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +2 Plate Mail is made of heavy dark metal plates. 1 / day while outside you may activate the armor as a Move Action by choosing a visible location within 50 feet. You shoot into the sky in a streak of flame. The next turn on your initiative you crash into the chosen location dealing 8d6 fire damage (DC 15 Dexterity save for half damage) to all units within 5 feet. Half damage to enemies with 15 feet."},{"n": "Toadskin","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "3 Charges","d": "This is a thin slightly wet set of +1 Hide Armor. As a reaction when you are struck by a melee attack, once per hour you may spend a charge to release a burst of poison DC 12 Constitution save or be poisoned for 1 minute. They may attempt to save again at the end of each round."},{"n": "Wooly Floof","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This armor was inspired by a mage who watch a sheep survive a strike from a giant's club due to it's excessive wool padding. This set of +2 Padded Armor is a clean white fluffy wool clothing with a hood that goes over the user's head and has a set of floppy sheep ears. Once per fall the user may immediately as a reaction mitigate all the fall damage but be bounced half the distance in the air maintaining any momentum they had previously. Additionally, once per day when struck by a bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing attack you may ignore the damage of the attack and instead of flung 1 ft per damage absorbed (round up to the nearest 5)"},{"n": "Bull Hide","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Hide or Leather armor allows the user to 1/day transform into a large Bull (see Cattle) for up to an hour gaining 40ft speed, 15 Temporary HP, and can deliver a charge attack that deals your weapon damage +2d6 damage and knocks an enemy prone on a failed DC13 Strength Check. Upon losing the temporary HP or"},{"n": "Cavalier's Guard","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This suit of +1 Half-Plate is expertly designed for riding. As a full round action when the user jumps in the air and spreads their legs apart an appropriately sized horse formed out of silver light appears almost instantly. This mount will vanish immediately upon death or it's dismounted. If slain it cannot be resummoned for 1 day"},{"n": "Deathbone Armor","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "Deathknights fashioned this armor laced with bones and sharp protrusions to equip on their most powerful frontline fighters so they would fight twice after falling in battle. This +1 Armor can be made from any Medium or Heavy Armor. The armor activates when the user is dying, the layer of bone falls off of the armor and forms a large skeleton which the dying player controls. (As Skeleton with Swordsword but Large, 30 HP, AC 14, Shortsword (+6 / 1d6+4 piercing damage). This effect ends when the Skeleton is reduced to 0 health or the user regains consciousness. After being activated this cannot be used again for 1d3 days."},{"n": "Fungicraft Armor","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "Fungicraft Armor is +2 Armor grown and fashioned from layers of wide mushrooms carefully crafted and spread across any Light Armor. Once a short rest the user may shake viciously releasing spores into the air. One round later these spores grow and morph into copies of user as the Mirror Image spell. When slain these explode into dangerous spores causing all enemies within 5 feet to take 2d4 poison damage (DC Con 12 for half damage)"},{"n": "Lifesense Heartpiece","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Breastplate has a small shimmer that spreads across it in tune with the users heartbeat. The user immediately senses the presence of any living creature tiny or larger than is within 5 feet of it. If the optional flanking rules are used the user cannot be flanked."},{"n": "Buoyant Armor","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This always wet armor can be fashioned from any suit of armor. It allows the wearer to float or sink as if the armor were heavy plate or made of air. The user can also hold their breath for up to 1 hour."},{"n": "Stoneplate","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Heavy Armor (any) is fashioned from stone instead of metal. When activated the armor turns the users skin to a thick granite granting the user the Stoneskin effect but their speed becomes 0ft. This effect may be ended at any time and cannot be used again until a long rest."},{"n": "Armor of Fangs","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This intimidating +1 Scale mail is covered in metal replica fangs of various beasts. When striking opponents the fangs can snap forward with the attack dealing additional damage or bite and close in on enemies that come too close to the user. This armor adds an additional +1 piercing damage to all unarmed attacks and whenever the user successfully grapples or is grappled this armor will deal 1d4 piercing damage to them."},{"n": "Armor of Repose","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Armor (any) has runes and markings of death in various languages carved in spaces across the armor. When dropped to 0 or less health the user automatically is stabilized and immediately is placed under the effect of a feign death spell appearing to have died immediately. This effect cannot be used again for 1d3 days."},{"n": "Armor of War","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Armor (any Medium) has a symbol of a deity of war forged onto the center of the armor. It grants the user 5 temporary hit points. These hit points are replenished any time the user slays an enemy in honorable combat."},{"n": "Stormeye Splint","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +3 Splint Armor causes light gusts of winds to constantly blow against and around the user. The armor gives the user the ability to Gust of Wind at will. It can also be activated to create a Tornado (as the spell) for 1 minute centered on the user. The user is immune to its effects. After using the Tornado none of its effects may be used until a long rest."},{"n": "Chargemetal Armor","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "7 Charges","d": "This +2 Armor (Metal only) grants the user immunity to Lightning Damage. You may cast Lightning Bolt for 1d6+1d6 damage per charge spent. This armor does not recharge naturally. Each 5 Lightning Damage absorbed (rounded up) gives the Armor 1 Charge."},{"n": "Trollskin Suit","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 thin skin tight green hide armor is a mix of off putting and also somewhat stylish. It clings to the users flesh and covers much more of the body than usual even the neck and palms. When the user is reduced to below half health the regeneration effect kicks in for the next 1 minute, healing the user 10 health at the start of each of their turns. Taking fire or acid damage disables the healing effect for 1 round. Additionally, once over the duration an arm or leg that has been severed while wearing the armor can be reattached. Once activated the effect can not be used again for 1 day."},{"n": "Acoustic Weave","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Padded armor is woven with all sorts of decorative and intentionally designed ornate shapes and patterns designed to amplify and reflect sound. Any instrument that is played to create bardic magic or use bardic inspiration that has a range gains an additional 50% range (Rounded up to the nearest 5 ft). Ex - Bardic Inspiration may be applied an ally within 90 feet (instead of 60) and thunderwave effects a 25 foot cone (instead of 15 ft)"},{"n": "The Dome","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Magic Stone Shield has the picture of a mountain carved into its center. It may be raised up as an action to turn into a dome of stone which is a 15 foot cube with the center point located next to the user. The dome has AC 15 and can take 60 damage before breaking apart and returning to the wielder. During this time the shield is removed from the user and they gain no benefit. This can be used once per long rest."},{"n": "Kinetic Shield","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "5 Charges","d": "This +1 Shield vibrates at a high frequency and keeping it steady requires a small amount of effort to maintain. This shield gains 1 charge each time you critically strike in melee or are critically struck against a dangerous opponent (DMs discretion). This shield gains 1d3 charges per day."},{"n": "Desert Skin Bracers","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "The bracers are well adapted to desert travel by absorbing the surrounding moisture to keep the owner alive. While worn you need only a tenth of the water needed as normal. Additionally, while grappling any enemy the armor attempts to steal moisture from them. Each turn while grappling they must make a DC 11 Constitution save or suffer 1 level of exhaustion."},{"n": "Bloodrage Armor","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This padded armor is treated as no-armor for the purposes of class features. When the user has less than 26 Strength and suffers damage from an attack they suffer an additional 1d4 damage but gain +2 Strength until end of combat."},{"n": "Righteous Bear Arms","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "These large furry sleeves are made of golden bear fur and the claws are infused with celestial fury and righteousness. They cover the wearer's arms granting them a Natural Armor of 11, +2 Strength (Max of 20) and giving them claw attacks that deal 1d10 damage. Additionally each unarmed or claw attack made with these weapons adds +1 radiant damage."},{"n": "Frozen Shield","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +1 Shield is cold to the touch. It grants the user frost resistance. Once per day the user may stun themselves in a giant block of ice as a reaction. The thick ice grants +50 temporary hp. This effect may be ended at the end of the user's turn or when the temporary hp is removed."},{"n": "Incubi's Vest","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This revealing leather armor must be worn without armor or additional coverage. You can cast Charm Person once per long rest. Whenever you grapple or are successfully grappled you deal 2d4 necrotic damage and heal half the damage dealt (DC12 Cha). Charmed creatures will automatically fail this save."},{"n": "Cosmic Hide","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +2 studded leather armor is made the sleek black leathery skin of a creature from a different plane. The studs are made from small shining pearls that glow lightly when the lights are dim. They swirl and slowly drift around the armor forming constellations and patterns. The armor grants proficiency in Religion and as a reaction the wearer may remove themselves from existence for 1 full turn. They are still visible via their outline, but they are not present for all purposes. On the wearers next turn they may only take a single move action. This feature is usable once per long rest."},{"n": "Wrappings of the Mummy","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +2 Padded armor is made of rigid cloth and bandages that cling tightly to the wearers skin. If reduced to below 0 health the wearer automatically stabilizes. It can also be activated or deactivated as a bonus action. When active any creature that begins its turn within 10 feet of the wearer suffer 2d8 necrotic damage (save 13 Con for half) and cannot benefit from any healing until their next turn."},{"n": "Ropeplate","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This +2 Ringmail is made of long strands of rope have been hardened and made stiff with sea water. When active the ropes flying out and entangle enemies, it may activate as an entangle spell within 10 feet of the user. The user also gains advantage on initiating a grapple check and can use it grab onto ledges within 30 feet granting advantage on checks involving climbing or swinging."},{"n": "Plated Superarmor","r": "","t": "Armor","u": "","d": "This set of +2 Fullplate grants the user +4 strength (Max of 22) and lowers their speed by 10. The armor itself is equipped with massive gauntlets connected to the back, any disarm attempts on the wielder fail automatically. The user can open or close these gauntlets with a bonus action to hold additional objects or weapons."},{"n": "Flaerrinton's Mercurial Solution","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This magical water tastes sweet but has no inherent properties. When mixed with a potion however it duplicates the properties of that potion creating two identical potions."},{"n": "Odh's Green Tea","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "For the next 24 hours all plants within 30 feet of the drinker grow rapidly as if affected by a Plant Growth spell, although it only slows units by half. The drinker's allies are unaffected by this effect."},{"n": "Elixir of Magic Resistance","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "When taken it grants the user as if they were under the effect of an anti-magic field for 10 minutes."},{"n": "Bottled Lightning","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "When taken it grants the user Lightning Armor (as Flame Armor but replace Fire with Lighting and Cold with Force) and their melee attacks deal an additional 1d8 lightning damage on hit for 1 minute."},{"n": "Sensual Slippery Soap","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "When used in a bath the user becomes incredibly clean for the next 24 hours. Their skin becomes soft and slippery granting advantage on all Dex Saves and the strong perfume from the soap grants advantage on Persuasion checks with creatures who can smell. Their smell however is strong enough that any creature trying to track or detect them has advantage on their checks due to the strong odor."},{"n": "Powder of Unmaking","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This potion when thrown or poured onto an object reverts the materials it is comprised of to its natural state. Glass turns to sand, metal to ore, wood to branches, food to its ingredients. If thrown on a creature it is allowed to make a Wisdom Save (DC12) to ignore the effects. Magical Items gain advantage on this save."},{"n": "Soldier Serum","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "These come in long thin red vials. When injected they gain +1 to Strength, Dexterity, and Constitution, as well as -2 Int, Wis, Charisma. This effect lasts for 10 hours. If used more than 3 times by the same target the effects become permanent."},{"n": "Soul of the Arbiter","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This elixir is the distilled magical essence of a legendary Monk. When consumed for the next 24 hours your personality changes to Lawful Neutral (though you're still you) your personality hardens and you find yourself incredibly calm and calculate and slow to ire. You find yourself unable to take hostile action against a creature who is not hostile towards you. You lose all class abilities and features and instead replace them with the class abilities of a Level 10 Monk (Way of the Open Hand) with twice the Ki charges. You have 12 Str, 20 Dex, 10 Con, 12 Int, 14 Wis, 10 Cha and 50 Temporary Health. If this health is reduced to 0 before the effect would normally end you revert to your original class and suffer 3d8 psychic damage."},{"n": "Soul of the Savage","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This elixir is the distilled magical essence of a horrific Marauder. When consumed for the next 24 hours your personality changes to Neutral Evil (though you're still you) your personality hardens and your have little space for mercy and compassion. When an enemy is dying you have a nigh irresistible urge to ensure they are finished before moving to the next one. You lose all class abilities and features and instead replace them with the class abilities of a Level 10 Barbarian (Berserker) with twice the number of rages. You have 20 Str, 14 Dex, 16 Con, 10 Int, 10 Wis, 8 Cha and 70 Temporary Health. If this health is reduced to 0 before the effect would normally end you revert to your original class and suffer 3d8 psychic damage."},{"n": "Soul of the Champion","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This elixir is the distilled magical essence of a great Champion. When consumed for the next 24 hours your personality changes to Neutral Good (though you're still you) your personality hardens and your have little space more mercy and compassion. When an enemy is dying you have a nigh irresistible urge to ensure they are finished before moving to the next one. You lose all class abilities and features and instead replace them with the class abilities of a Level 10 Fighter (Battlemaster) with twice the number of superiority dice. You have 16 Str, 16 Dex, 14 Con, 12 Int, 12 Wis, 14 Cha and 60 Temporary Health. If this health is reduced to 0 before the effect would normally end you revert to your original class and suffer 3d8 psychic damage."},{"n": "Elixir of Profuse Sweating","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "When drunk this elixir causes the user to sweat profusely for an hour. They gain resistance to Fire and Cold and advantage on escaping any grapple checks."},{"n": "God's Healing Elixir","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This is a healing potion meant to restore catastrophic wounds for gods and demigods, while powerful, it isn't meant for mortal consumption. Once drunk the user heals for 40% of their maximum health each round for the next minute. Each time the user is healing to full or more they gain 1 level of exhaustion. At the end of the effect the user suffers 1 stage of exhaustion and 3d8 damage."},{"n": "Animal Snax","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "These delicious protein treats can be used to Animal Friendship on a non-hostile beast. If successful it will eat the snack and benefit from the Enlarge and has advantage on all skill checks for the next hour."},{"n": "Sphere of Insanity","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "When this glass sphere is distilled lquid chaotic energy from the outer planes. When smashed it explodes in a burst of light and colors. All creatures within 150 feet are blinded for 1 minute, they are allowed a save at the end of each round to end the effect (Con Save DC 16). Each creature must also make a Wisdom Save (DC 17 or have their soul sucked from their body). Each creature that got their soul sucked out has enters a random available body that also failed its save for 1 minute. If either the creatures original body or their current body is slain the creature perishes."},{"n": "Bear Claw","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This delicious pastry when consumed transforms the user into a Bear/Human hybrid (gaining 20 Strength, a 1d10 dmg bite attack and 2 1d8 claw attacks, and Keen Smell) -or- into a DireBear for the next 8 hours. If regurgitated, the effect can end early but will not end early otherwise."},{"n": "Bloodhound Juice","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This slightly sweet beverage gives the user an accute sense of smell granting them Keen Sense (Smell) for 12 hours. Additionally, if a piece of blood, clothing, or any object is dropped into the potion the drinker can sense their presence and rough direction as long as they are within a mile."},{"n": "Potion of Extreme Belching","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "The drinker belch a gigantic beltch in a 15 foot cone. This knocks the drinker back 15 feet and all units in the cone back 15 feet as well unless a Strength Save (DC13 is made)"},{"n": "Zombification","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This potion when drank or thrown at an enemy grants the unit the Undead trait for 10 minutes if they fail their Con Save (DC 14). If affected, the user takes damage from healing spells and heals from necrotic damage."},{"n": "Elixir of Death","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This potion when drunk kills the user for 10 minutes which the drinker may resist with a DC15 Con Save."},{"n": "Pain Reducer","r": "","t": "Potion","u": "","d": "This distilled elixir reduces the feeling and impact of pain on the user. This effect lasts for 10 minutes. The user cannot take more than 10% of their maximum health in damae in a given round. Instead any damage over 10% is delayed and applied on the following turn. At the end of this effect the user suffers a level of exhaustion."},{"n": "Ring of Arrow Deflection","r": "Rare","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "(Attunement) +1 AC. Projectiles are repelled by this ring like a powerful magnet bending and twisting their trajectory to avoid the wielder. Any time a missile attack misses you by 5 or more and a valid enemy unit is within 10 feet of you, the attacker must roll the attack against that enemy instead."},{"n": "Cantrip Focus Ring","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring comes loaded with a cantrip from the Sorcerer spell list. A non-Sorcerer using this ring may use that cantrip once per short rest. A Sorcerer may use this cantip as if it were their own. Additionally they deal +1 damage on all Cantrip attacks."},{"n": "Ring of Spell Absorption","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring may be activated as a reaction when a spell is being cast within 30 feet. If the caster doesn't pass a Wisdom Save (DC14) they must target this ring wearer is possible. Failing this save by more than 5 means the spell is absorbed and also rendered harmless and the ringbearer gains temporary health equal to the spell level x2 (Cantrips count as 1). This ring can successfully retarget 1 spell per day."},{"n": "Ring of Undying Fury","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This red ring painfully digs itself into the wearers skin in combat causing the wearers hand to bleed. Once per day when activated the ring increases the users Strength granting +1d4 damage on all melee attacks for 1 minute. While active if damage would drop drop the user to 0 hp they instead are reduced to 1 health and must make a Constitution save with a DC equal to the damage dealt or this effect then ends immediately. If the wearer of this ring is slain this ring fades losing its power forever"},{"n": "Fey Spirit Ring","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This powerful ring binds and controls small fey spirits of battle and conflict. The ring starts with no spirits bound, but during combat or at inopportune times a fey spirit or two that is visible only to the caster appears. It will observe the conflict with interest but flee if approached. If successfully grappled they are bound to the ring giving it one more maximum charge to a Maximum of 10. These charges refresh at dawn or when a new spirit is captured. The spirits escape the ring at a rate of 1 per week. Charges may be expended to... Cast Faerie Fire (1 Charge) Cast Invisibility (2 Charges) Switch the positions of Two creatures within 15 feet of each other. (3 Charges) Release the Spirits - deal 1d4 psychic damage per Spirit randomly to enemies within 30 feet. Each spirit has a 50% chance of continuing to fight next round repeating this effect. (X Charges)"},{"n": "The Resilience of Earth","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring grants the user 18 Constitution if it is not already higher. You gain a Burrow Speed of 5 feet and +1 to your AC. You gain Mold Earth and Resilience as Cantrips and once per day may cast Stoneskin on yourself."},{"n": "The Fury of Flame","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring grants the user 18 Strength if it is not already higher. You gain Immunity to Fire Damage. You gain Sacred Flame and Control Flames as Cantrips and can cast Fireball once per day."},{"n": "The Grace of Air","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring grants the user 18 Dexterity if it is not already higher. You gain Evasion as a Rogue and +2 to your Initiative. You also gain Gust as a Cantrip and once per day may cast Flight on yourself."},{"n": "The Serenity of Water","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring grants the user 18 Wisdom and Intelligence if they are not already higher. You gain proficiency in all Saving throws. Additionally you may breath underwater and gain a swim speed of 50 feet. You gain Ray of Frost and Shape Water as cantrips and can cast Wall of Ice once per day."},{"n": "The Eternity of Spirit","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring grants the user 18 Charisma if it is not already higher. You can communicate Telepathically with any willing creature within 30 feet. You gain the Vicious Mockery Spell as a Cantrip. Once per day you may cast True Seeing on yourself."},{"n": "Ring of Fireflies","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "In any natural environment you can concentrate and draw nearby fireflies to circle near you. These flies make you easy to spot but illuminate the 15 ft area around you. Additionally these flies will turn from yellow to red when hostile creatures are nearby. The flies can also keep watch and alert the wielder is they are resting. They have a perception score of +2, with advantage on anything within 10 feet of the wearer."},{"n": "Ring of Reasonable Wishes","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This somewhat beautiful silver ring has slots for 3 opals configured in a triangle pattern, though no ring is ever made with all 3. Each opal present grants the user one wish from a wispy spirit that inhabits the ring. When activated the spirit will try its best to fulfill the wish but it only has the power level of any 5th level spellcaster, of the type most appropriate for the needs of the wish. When the ring is expened of wishes it can still be used once per day, but the Spirits power will have been reduced to a level 1 spellcaster."},{"n": "Ring of Retrieval","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "When the wearer takes a long rest they may attune their current equipement to the ring. As a bonus action the user may immediately teleport some or all of their gear onto their person as long as it exists on the same plane of existence"},{"n": "Ring of the Betrothed","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "These magic rings come in sets. When attuned the two wearers must hold hands and recite bonds of fealty and bonding. While within a mile of one another they both gain +1 to all saving throws, +1 AC. If either wearer either removes or break attunement they both suffer the effects of Bestow Curse (Wisdom save or waste their action from heartbreak) until they rebond."},{"n": "Ring of Temptation","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This magic ring appears to be a Ring of the Betrothed. It grants its user the ability to cast Charm Person once per day. If the attunement ceremony is held with a creature wearing the Ring of the Betrothed they gain all the benefits of the Ring instead of it's original owner. If the wearer of the Ring of the Betrothed ever leaves the 1 mile radius of the owner of the Ring of Temptation they suffer the effects of the curse, though their partner does not."},{"n": "Riding Whistle","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This beautiful wooden ring has the symbol of a horse. It can cast Animal Friendship once per day that has advantage of creatures that would be excellent mounts (DMs discretion). The ring can also be blown to call a befriended mount within 1 mile to immediately run to the owner at twice their normal speed."},{"n": "Ring of the Mother Spider","r": "","t": "Ring","u": "","d": "This ring when worn for a period of time adheres to the users finger. When removed a magical string of spider silk is connected between the ring and the wearers finger. This string is not physical and becomes invisible shortly after being revealed. Both users can climb with a speed of 15 ft. Additionally, when the ring is now worn by another individual the two wearers are bound. If the new wielder is struck by any damaging ability, you automatically cast Web at the attacker and gain 10 temporary HP. This cannot be triggered more than once per day"},{"n": "Scepter of the Damned Army","r": "","t": "Rod","u": "10 Charges","d": "This +2 Mace when raised in an outdoor area can summon Medium Skeletons or Zombies wearing the tattered uniforms of their former lives that claw their way out of the ground over 1 minute. These Undead last for 1 hour and will obey general instructions from the user (Attack, Move, Defend, Stop). The Scepter summons a number of creatures equal to the number of charges spent multiplied by the number of charges spent (1 Charge summons 1 Skeletons or Zombies, 6 Charges summons 36, 10 Charges summons 100). Any Large creature or smaller slain by this Mace is resurrected as a Skeleton or Zombie under the wielder's control. This lasts for 1 hour. The Rod recharges 1d3-1 charges per day."},{"n": "Slow Cooker","r": "","t": "Rod","u": "","d": "This heavy rod is made of enchanted charcoal and seems to stir with an internal heat and embers. As an action you may make a spell attack by shooting a beam of heat energy at an enemy within 30 feet dealing 1d6 fire damage. Each round you use this weapon in a row increases the damage by another 1d6, to a maximum of 10d6 total damage. If you attempt to use the Rod while after it has reached maximum damage it will explode as a Fireball spell with the spell centered on the user and go innert for 1 week."},{"n": "Multitool","r": "","t": "Rod","u": "","d": "This straightforward looking metal and wooden rod can twist and seperate hiding all sorts of useful tools It contains all of the reusable tools present in a Thieves Tools, Crafters Kit, or Explorers Kit."},{"n": "Rod of Electrical Control","r": "","t": "Rod","u": "","d": "This two section part, adamantine rod. The top portion of the rod be fired as a ranged attack with a range of 15/30 feet. Upon hit it deals 1d4 lightning damage imbeds itself in their body and they make a Wisdom Save (DC14). If it fails for the next minute they are paralyzed, but you can spend your move action moving and turning the bottom section of the rod to make the enemy move in that direction at half lurching speed. You can spend your action you can make them make a basic attack. Any turn you force it to take an action grants it an opportunity to save and deals it 1d4 lightning damage"},{"n": "Scroll of Magic for Dunces","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This magic scroll when read grants the cantrip on the scroll to the user for 24 hours."},{"n": "Note of Repayment","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This scroll can be used in place of payment for any creature that fails a Charisma save DC 20 (-1 for each 50 gold requested). If failed the creature will accept the note in place of value equaling the requested amount. They will fully expect the next time they meet the user to be repaid if at least 1 day has passed since it was offered."},{"n": "Martial Technique","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "These scrolls can be read an an action. They can use a single Manuever as a Fighter (Battlemaster) for the next hour and grants the reader two d6 'superiority dice'"},{"n": "Autocartrographer","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This blank map when activated becomes clear. As you progress through a dungeon or town the scroll will begin to automatically fill out a map."},{"n": "Trivial Scroll","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This rolled up scroll comes wrapped with a string and a wax seal. It won't open unless a question about a non-living creature, place, or event is asked. When opened the scroll will contain the answer."},{"n": "Infiniscroll","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This scrollcase has the edge of the paper emerging from one side. It can be pulled to reveal more and more paper. There is no limit to the volume of paper that can be pulled from the scrollcase."},{"n": "Siphoning Scroll","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This scroll if accessible can be read as a reaction and can be used when any creature within 60 feet who is visible is using a scroll. When read the magic of scroll will transfer into this item and be read instead of the original. This is consumed on use."},{"n": "Ninja Scroll","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This cursed scroll has a thin razor spike on the end of it. It conceals this weapon and tries to hide and blend in with other scrolls. When any creature exposes their back to the Ninja Scroll it will jump up and shank them making an attack at +6 to hit, with advantage if it's surprising the enemy. This attack deals 1d4 piercing +2d6 sneak attack damage. Immediately after it tries to hide back in the scrolls before anybody notices the attack. It has a hide skill of +11."},{"n": "Decree of Law","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This scroll when activated places a rule of law within 100 feet of the caster, which must be defined by the caster. The rules must be generic and easily understood enough that any intellegent creature can follow them. \"Do not gang up on an enemy\" \"Do not get hit with an attack\" \"Do not move more than 5 feet a turn\" all qualify. Any intelligent creature that breaks the rule must make a DC14 WIsdom Save or suffer 3d8 psychic damage. The creature is always aware on any action that would break a rule."},{"n": "Scroll of Repetition","r": "","t": "Scroll","u": "","d": "This powerful spell when used resonates and blasts a creature within 90 feet with powerful magic. If the target fails a DC 14 Wisdom Save, any attack, spell, or effect they suffer, good or bad, is duplicated on the following turn."},{"n": "The Nope Stick","r": "","t": "Staff","u": "3 Charges","d": "This +2 Quarterstaff is made of gnarled wood. It leaves particularly hideous bruises and scars where it hits.Additionally the wielder may yell \"Shut Up\" or \"Stop Staring\" or \"No Running!\" with a DC 14 Con Save or be inflicted with Silence, Blinded, or Immobilize Respectively for 1 minute. The enemy may make an additional save at the end of their turn. Charges refresh at dawn."},{"n": "Staff of the Storm","r": "","t": "Staff","u": "10 Charges","d": "This staff has 10 charges with 1d4 recharging each dawn. 1 Charge may be use on hit to deal an additional 1d8+3 Lightning Damage. 3 Charges may be used to chain lightning dealing 2d8 Lightning Damage to an enemy within 30 ft. This effect can bounce to any additional creature within 15 feet (Dex Save 13 for half), you may bounce to any number of creatures and Teleport next to the last target. 5 Charges can be expended to cast Lightning Bolt."},{"n": "Staff of Hail","r": "","t": "Staff","u": "","d": "This +2 Quarterstaff deals an additional 1d8 ice damage on strike. Additionally you may activate or deactivate a SleetStorm effect, centered on the wielder with a range of 15 feet once per day lasting up to 10 minutes. The wielder is unaffected."},{"n": "Pitfall Shovel","r": "","t": "Staff","u": "","d": "This Shovel functions as a +1 Quarterstaff. It has the ability to spend a charge to dig a 5 foot by 5 foot hole as a full round action - or you can spend 1 charge to dig it as a bonus action. It may expend 2 charges to instead dig 5 5x5 holes in any configuration as long as they are all connected. 1 Charge is regained each dawn, unless it is buried in which case it recharges 1d4+1 charges."},{"n": "Oaken Staff of the Treant","r": "","t": "Staff","u": "10 Charges","d": "This large +2 Staff. While holding it you can spend 1 charge as a bonus action to turn it into a large tree-like club (complete with leaves), which is treated as a Greatclub but deals 2d6 Bludgeoning Damage. You may also spend X Charges to cast Animate plants but create X Medium Size or smaller plants. This staff regains 1d4 charges at dawn, doubled if you rest outside."},{"n": "Staff of Snakes","r": "","t": "Staff","u": "9 Charges","d": "This twisted staff resembles a serpent and when watched seems to slowly twist and curl at an almost impercievable rate. Upon striking an enemy-, the wielder may spend a charge to force the enemy to make a DC 12 Con save or the struck limb is changed into a snake. The snake will not attack its owner but it will not help them either rendering the limb functionally useless until a Remove Curse spell is cast. The wielder may additionally summon a Giant Constrictor Snake for 1 hour at the cost of 3 charges. The staff recharges 1d3 charges per day which increases to 1d4+1 if there a snake nearby when it rests."},{"n": "Wand of Instant Regret","r": "","t": "Wand","u": "7 Charges","d": "When an enemy within 60 feet fails a skill check or saving throw, as an action you may spend a charge from this item to blast them with magical humiliation dealing 1d4+1 force damage. As a reaction you may also spend 3 charges when an opponent rolls a natural 1 to blast them with energy dealing 2d8+3 force damage. The want recharges 1d3 charges per day."},{"n": "Wand of Hidden Truths","r": "","t": "Wand","u": "3 Charges","d": "When cast at a target they must make a Charisma Save DC 12 or say a sentence out loud that they really didn't want others around them to hear (DM's discretion). The user may make a Deception roll vs Perception to use this ability without causing suspicion. This item regains 1 charge at dawn."},{"n": "Wand of the Glutton","r": "","t": "Wand","u": "5 Charges","d": "You may spend a charge to make a ranged attack roll. If successful it deals 1d6 + 1d6 force damage for each charge spent. Then if the creature has less hp remaining than 1d6 per charge spent they are polymorphed into the food item of your choice. This wand regains 1d3 charges each morning."},{"n": "Wand of Nightmares","r": "","t": "Wand","u": "7 Charges","d": "This wand has several abilities. It can spend 1 charge to cast Sleep on a single creature. It can also instill Nightmares for 2 charges in a sleeping creature dealing 3d6 psychic damage (Wisdom Save DC 12 to wake up - though damage is still taken), or spend 2 charges to cast Minor Image on a single enemy (DC 12) with disadvantage if they are sleeping."},{"n": "Wand of Tears","r": "","t": "Wand","u": "5 Charges","d": "When used you can expend a charge and point the wand at a creature within 30 feet. They must pass a Cha Save DC12 or begin to gently cry for 1 minute giving them disadvantage on all Charisma checks and saves. If they are struck again they begin to sob uncontrollably losing the ability to speak properly and moving at half speed. If struck successfully a third time they fall to the ground hands clutching their head and are immobilized. Taking damage will immediately end this effect, though tears will still flow. This item regains 1d2 charges each dawn."},{"n": "Pitchfork of Revolution","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This Pitchfork behaves as a Trident +1 and is stained with the blood, sweat, and tears of revolution. When raised once per week it casts Mass Suggestion (DC 14 Save) with the following differences. The effect can target 24 characters and only lasts 1 hour. All targets gain advantage on the saving throw if the suggestion is anything that isn't 'revolutionary' ie anything opposing their current social hierarchy, laws, or structure."},{"n": "Blade of Alarm","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "A +1 Dagger or Scimitar. When drawn and a hostile entity is within 60 feet the blade emits a single horrible scream."},{"n": "Scythe of the Damned","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "A +1 Scythe. When it kills an enemy, the corpse immediately rises and you may make it do a single move and attack action on your turn as a bonus action, before once again returning to rest"},{"n": "Vinelash","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "An Emerald +1 whip covered in leaf motifs. When activate it extend the length of the whip to 30 feet."},{"n": "Chef Knife","r": "Uncommon","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "A Masterwork dagger simple that is simple and elegant in design. When it cuts meat it perfectly cooks it, when cutting flesh it deals an additional 1d3 fire damage as it cooks them. The cuts smell delicious and well seasoned."},{"n": "Stilleto of Possession","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "A horrific assassin's blade. It is a +1 Rapier that deals an additional 1d4 necrotic damage on hit. If it kills an enemy you may possess that creature's body, rendering your previous form lifeless."},{"n": "Fork of Furious Stabbing","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This is a large three pronged rusty metal fork. It's a +1 magical 1d2 damage simple weapon. Each time in combat you succeed at wounding an opponent the weapon increases its damage die until the end of combat. The die increases from 1d2 > 1d3 > 1d4 > 1d6 > 1d8 > 1d10 > 2d6 > 2d8. The metal on the weapon begins to change from rusted iron to a dark crimson with each successful stab."},{"n": "Butcher's Knife","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This serrated +1 Knife thirsts to slay it's enemies and excels at cutting through flesh. It was created by a murderer known only as the butcher. If it reduces a foe below 0 hp may immediately make another free attack with this weapon. Any downed enemy or corpse struck by this knife is carved up into as if they were properly butched. If alive they are slain instantly."},{"n": "Portal Bow","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "1/day you may Teleport to the square shot by this attack. You may also attack an empty tile as if AC 15. If the attack misses the DM may place you up to 5 feet away for each point the attack failed by."},{"n": "Bolts of Madness","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "Ammo","d": "When used this crossbow bolt upon hitting a target forces the target to make a DC 13 will save or go berserk attacking the closest unit friend or foe with their melee weapon. They may remake this save at the end of each round."},{"n": "Boltsurge Crossbow","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "7 Charges","d": "This +1 heavy crossbow can be activated to fire additional arrows with an attack. Any number of charges may be expended. If a charge is spent the attack hits deal an additional 1d4 damage plus an additional 1d4 for each charge spent. Killing an enemy with this weapon immediately grants d3 charges."},{"n": "Blades of the Huntsman","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "Created for Bounty Hunters to hunt and catch their prey this +1 silver throwing knife can be commanded at any point to split into three identical blades. This effect removes any other duplicates that have been made previously. The user gains knowledge of where any of these knives are as per the Locate Object spell. If the object is out of range the user may still inquire it's location but may only get the general direction once per hour."},{"n": "Tordle's Explosive Mushrooms","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These mushrooms when thrown will stick and adhere to any surface. When a unit moves onto their square they explode dealing 6d6 poison damage and blinding all enemies within 5 feet for 1 round (Save DC14 Con for Half damage and no blind)"},{"n": "Dart's of Eternal Love","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These +1 Pink Heart shaped Darts charm (DC11 Wis) when hit for 1d3+1 rounds as Charm Person. Getting hit with subsequent darts does not break the effect and causes the opponent to have disadvantage on the saving throw."},{"n": "Mageseeker's Talon","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 shortsword when held allows the user to cast detect magic at will. Additionally it gains a charge per spell level (min1) each time a spell is cast by an enemy within 60 feet. This blade can cast Dispel Magic for 3 charges -or- when striking an enemy who can cast spells with this item deal an additional +1d4 psychic damage per charge expended. These charges are lost at the end of each day."},{"n": "Glacialfreeze Bow","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Shortbow is chill to the touch. As arrows are loaded into this bow they become covered in ice and wispy trails of cold eminante from the arrows. Enemies struck by an arrow must make a DC 13 Con Save or lose -10 speed for the next 2 rounds as crystals of ice form begin to form across their body. While active each time an additional arrow hits and a save is failed the speed reduction stacks and the effect is refreshed. When a creature is reduced to 0 speed in this manner the ice completes and shatters. Incapacitating the creature for 1 turn and dealing 1d8 ice damage for each stack of the effect."},{"n": "The Party Whip","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 whip when hitting a creature forces them to make a DC13 Charisma Save or become incapacitated with dancing for 1 round. A creature may only fail this save once a day."},{"n": "Duelists' Blade","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Dagger has a larger than normal guard that is designed to catch and twist opponent's attacks. If you don't perform an attack with this weapon on your turn it grants +2 to AC against attacks from melee weapons. If a melee attack misses you by 2 or less you may spend your reaction to make a free attack with this blade."},{"n": "Showman's Axe","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Throwing Axe bounces back to the user upon being thrown. It can be caught and flourished with an acrobatics check DC equal to half the total distance moved after Throwing the Axe. If you catch the axe your next attack this combat from this weapon gains an additional 1d4 damage per 10 feet moved."},{"n": "Soul Render's Grasp","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Whip drips with necromancy magic. Thin white wispy tendrils trail from the weapon. You may make grapple checks at reach with this item. When you succeed at a grapple check they must make a DC 14 Wisdom Save. If failed it will pull a spirit of that creature into your adjacent square lasting 1d3+1 rounds. This creature has the identical HP, AC, and saving throws as the original creature and is tethered to it's parent. The tether is broken when the spirit is slain or the creature moves more than 30 feet from the Spirit (The creature is aware of a ramifications of leaving). If the tether is broken the creature is cursed as if a Bestow Curse spell has been cast on them (they do not get a save vs this effect). Damaging the Spirit deals half that damage to the original creature (rounded down). This may have no effect on creatures without a spirit such as Constructs(DMs discretion)"},{"n": "Dwarven Handcannon of Patience","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Metal Hand Crossbow has dwarven runes along the edges of the main shaft. Each time a shot is fires these runes light up blazing with an ember like red fire. After firing 3 shots the runes are all aglow and the weapon will begin to hum and shine for the next minute. The 4th shot will be incredibly powerful and add an additional 2d6 to the weapon's damage and add substantial recoil to the shot and the runes reset. If the magic expires naturally before being fired the crossbow shakes and explodes outwards with magic dealing 2d6 damage to the holder and becoming inert (just a regular hand crossbow) for 1d4 days."},{"n": "Echo Wraps","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These hand wrappings add +1 to attack rolls with unarmed attacks. Each time the user hits with an unarmed attack lands you gain blindsense 20ft for 1 round."},{"n": "Blade of Radiance","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 sword when draws casts Sunlight as the spell. Additionally the first time it hits a target it bathes the enemy in Light, mimicking the effects of Faerie Fire"},{"n": "Hammers of Light","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These +1 Light Hammers are used by the Holy War Clerics and often found in multiples. They are for Clerics who used to be warriors turned healers. Once per long rest each hammer may be used to heal as though it was a Cure Light Wounds spell instead of dealing damage. If thrown an attack roll is still required, though a willing target may forgo their Shield or Dexterity bonus to AC."},{"n": "Hunting Blade","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Shortsword may once per short rest apply Hunter's Mark on any enemy it hits. This mark lasts for 10 minutes and may not be transferred if the unit dies."},{"n": "The PentaGauntlet","r": "Artifact","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This powerful artifact is a gauntlet of immense size meant for a giant, but will resize itself to the user when attuned. It's a powerful weapon +3 Gauntlet dealing 2d8 damage. Additionally when attuned you gain the benefits of each Ring of Resilience of Earth, Fury of Flame, Grace of Air, Serenity of Water, and Eternity of Spirit worn on the gauntlet without using one of your attunement slots. Additionally each ring's once per day spell become at-will spells instead."},{"n": "Knife of Wind","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Knife adds an additional 1d6 thunder damage on hit and may push an opponent 5 ft in any direction. Additionally when making an attack action you may move up to 10 feet without provoking an attack of opportunity. You also gain +10 Speed."},{"n": "Axe of Lightning","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Battleaxe deals an additional 1d12 Lightning Damage on hit. When striking any target this weapon deals 1d12 lightning damage to an additional enemy within 15 feet. (Dex Save DC15 for half damage). Once per day you may also cast Lightning Bolt"},{"n": "The Storm Herald","r": "Artifact","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +3 Halberd is made of the combined Staff of Hail, the Axe of Lightning, and the Knife of Wind. It deals an additional 1d6 force, 1d8 ice, and 1d12 lightning damage. The 1d6 force, 1d8 ice, and 1d12 lightning damage also apply to an enemy within 15 feet (Dex save DC16 for half) This weapon can activate a Storm Sphere effect at will. Additionally you gain +10 speed and immunity to Lightning, Ice, and Thunder Damage."},{"n": "Winged Arrows","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These arrows have very large guide feathers. When fired they soar pulling along whatever they are attached to. The user may target an empty tile with AC 15. Each 1 they miss by moves the arrow 1 tile (DMs discretion) These can pull a large creature half the distance of the shot. Unwilling creatures are allowed a Strength Save (DC 14) . Once fired this arrow becomes inert for 1d3 days."},{"n": "Crystalline Sling","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This Sling was created by Gnomes to capture the magic within gemstones. When throwing gems it is treated as a +2 sling. When it throws gems of 50 gold value or higher these explode on impact with the enemy dealing an additional 2d4 elemental damage based on the type of gemstone use and deal this damage to all enemies within 5 feet (Dex Save DC 13 to avoid). If a gem of over 100 gold of value is used this damage is increased to 2d8. Examples of gem damage types below (DMs discretion if other gems are used). Each gem can only be used once ever in this fashion, but it is not consumed and does not lose value. Sapphire - Ice Ruby - Fire Diamond - Force Topaz - Lightning Emerald - Poison Onyx - Acid"},{"n": "Devastating Bottle","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 glass club is full of decent liquor. When attacking an enemy if it hits they must make a Con Save (DC 11) or be stunned for 1 round. This weapon then becomes functionally a +1 scimitar from the remaining shards. This weapon deals triple damage on a critical hit instead of double."},{"n": "Golden Knuckles of Freedom","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These gold metal knuckles were used by a rebellious monk who was fighting against a corrupt king who was overtaxing and stealing from his people. When he went to defend the peasants these knuckles were infused with the missing and stolen money. As he beat up the oppressors he spilled coins into the street and the people rejoiced. The knuckles spell C-H-A-R-I-T-Y-! with one letter inscribed on each knuckle. These count as magical attacks and grant a +1 bonus to unarmed attacks. Additionally each unarmed attack that hits its target causes 1d4 gold coins to fly from the targets body. Critical strikes cause 6d6 gold to fly from their body. The user cannot collect these coins and cannot use the money there to cheat any additional share of treasure or loot. If they do so the knuckles deactivate never working again for the user."},{"n": "Shockstick","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Morning Star adds an additional 1d8 lightning damage on each strike. Up to 3 times per day it may be supercharged adding an additional 2d8 lightning damage -or- if used on a target below 0 health it stabilizes them immediately bringing them to 1 health and granting them 3d8 temporary health for the next minute."},{"n": "Crow Bar","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Black Iron Club is covered with Raven and Crows feathers. It grants advantage on Animal Handling checks with crows and ravens and any check to open a chest or box. When you strike an enemy with this weapon it summons a crow that proceeds to peck them at the end of their turn. There can be any number of crows they have 1 hp and AC 12, These deal 1 damage per crow if they fail their save (DC 12 Dexterity save)."},{"n": "Boulder of Surprise","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This small stone can be thrown or launched from a sling. When the word is spoken it expands into a massive boulder 6 feet in diameter. This deals 6d6 damage (Dex Save 13 for half damage). It remains in its giant size until the word is spoken again. It cannot be enlarged more than once per hour."},{"n": "Injector","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 hand crossbow fires thin glass vials and made famous by the Alchemist Galeca who wielded two with great effectiveness applying bonuses and poison's across the battlefield shooting friends and foes alike. It is weaker than a normal bow and does not add your ability modifier to damage. It can however be loaded with any potion, poison, or liquid and apply it as an injection on hit. If the arrow misses it's target it may be retrieved and can be used again."},{"n": "Traitor's Blade","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "5 Charges","d": "This +1 Short automatically critically strikes when it hits any creature that does not treat the user as hostile. The user may also expend a charge to add +1d6 to any sneak attack damage the user can use. The blade also grants the user proficiency in Persuasion."},{"n": "Terrorhook","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "3 Charges","d": "This +1 sickle can transform into a creature's worst nightmare and deepest fear. Spending a charge transforms the weapon visually into something that truly scares the target adding 1d4 necrotic damage to each attack. On a successful hit this effect can be expended to cause them to be frightened (DC Wisdom 14), if the attack is a critical strike the save has disadvantage. This recharges 1d3 charges per day."},{"n": "Quipper Needler","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "7 Charges","d": "This +2 hand crossbow has sharp fins along the bow. It is coarse and rough with salt and allows the user to shoot underwater with no penalty. Additionally, it can expend 1 charge to fire a Quipper instead of an arrow. The Quipper can smell blood and has advantage on any enemy with less than half health. Upon impact it deals an additional 1d4 bleeding damage and they must make a save at the end of each turn (DC14 Constitution) or suffer an additional 1d4 bleeding damage. This bleed damage increases by 1d4 each time it strikes the same unit. 1 Charge is restored each dawn, which is increased to 1d4+1 if it is submerged and rests in water for at least 8 hours."},{"n": "Shark Cannon","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "5 Charges","d": "This +3 heavy crossbow is covered in sharkskin and has a large shark fin that functions as a sight along the top of the stock. It can fire underwater with no penalty. It can also expend 1 charge to fire a Reef Shark dealing 2d10 base damage or spend 3 charges to fire a Giant Shark, dealing 4d10 base damage. This Shark is allied to the user and will do its best to fight for them. If fired on land the Shark has a walk speed of 5 ft and will expire after 1 minute. 1 Charge is restored each dawn which is increased to 1d3+1 if it is submerged and rests in salt water for at least 8 hours."},{"n": "Curse Eater","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This morning star was forged in a temple and bathed in starlight and it's head formed from starmetal. It functions as a +2 morningstar, it deals an additional 1d8 radiant damage against Undead, Aberrations. It can once per day also be used to cast Consume Curse. This functions as Remove Curse but it also empowers the weapon for 24 hours with +1d8 necrotic damage against all targets."},{"n": "Skylancers Pike","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "10 Charges","d": "This +1 Pike is a weapon favored by Paladins on mount and on the ground. As a bonus action you may spend any number of charges. Until the end of the round this weapon adds +10 feet to it's reach, and +1 piercing damage to all attacks, for each charge consumed. This weapon regains 1d3 charges per day."},{"n": "Flourishing Rapier","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Rapier gives it's user +1 superiority dice if they have any. If not, once per day it can attempt to disarm an opponent and they must pass a strength save (DC 12) or drop a chosen object. Anytime the user disarms an opponent with this weapon they may immediately make an attack with the dropped object as a reaction though the object still ends up at the owners feet."},{"n": "Hookboots","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "These impressive boots are made of the chitin of a powerful beast and have hooked blades on each side designed after a Hook horrors natural weapons. These are +1 exotic weapons with Light, Monk, Finesse, and deal 1d6 damage each. They also grant advantage on Athletic checks to climb."},{"n": "Fang of Corruption","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +3 Sickle is made from the tooth of a Black Dragon great Wyrm and forged into the hilt is a ruby that is phylactory of a once powerful lich. Animals shun the presence of the wielder and plants within 5 feet wither and die on their approach. On striking an enemy this weapon deals an additional 1d8 Acid damage and 3d6 Necrotic damage. This Necrotic damage cannot be healed in any way without a Remove Curse spell. You may also cast Acid Spray at will, this spell has a 1d4+1 round recharge time after casting."},{"n": "Arm of DarkIce","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +3 Mace is made of a core of bone from a great wyrm White dragon and then covered in dark blue ice. This weapon automatically critically strikes against a full health enemy. This weapon deals an additional 2d4 Ice Damage and 2d4 necrotic damage on hit and the enemy must pass a Dex Save of freeze over becoming immobile for 1 round. Any enemy killed by this weapon becomes frozen and encased in dark ice. Striking a frozen target with this weapon is an automatic critical hit and shatters them creating a cone of cold in the direction of the attack. ."},{"n": "Spiked Tail of Inferno","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +3 Whip is made from the tail spike, sinew, and scales of an a Great Wyrm Red dragon. It has a reach of 15 feet and upon striking a target they must pass a Dex Save (DC15) or catch fire taking 2d6 damage each turn. They may spend a move action to attempt another save against this damage. For each tile or creature currently on fire this weapon adds an 1d6 fire damage upon hit."},{"n": "Claw of Venom","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +3 Handaxe is made from the claws of a Green Dragon great wyrm. This weapon deals an additional 2d6 poison damage on hit and they must make a DC14 Con Save or suffer the effects of venom (see below) for 1 minute. As a bonus action the wielder can switch what type of venom drips from the blade. The following types of Venom is available. Blinding - Suffers Blind Poisoned - Suffers Poisoned Painful - Suffers 2d6 additional poison damage each round Crippling - Reduces speed by 75% Deadly - If the user suffers from 2 other types of Venom they die instantly."},{"n": "Horn of Storm","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +3 Spear is made from the horn of a Blue Dragon great wyrm. It deals an additional 2d6 lightning damage on hit that can also strike any number of enemies within 10 feet of each other and be paralyed for 1 round (Dex Save DC 13 to avoid both effects). The user may fire a lightning bolt at any target hit by the lightning damage which strikes from the sky at the start of their next turn. After casting this has a has a 1d4 round recharge time."},{"n": "Warpstar","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Morning Star can teleport the up to 10 feet as long as you end in range of your target. Additionally, as a Reaction once per day, the wielder can teleport 10 feet in any direction."},{"n": "Club of Celebratation","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 club upon critically striking or killing an enemy will cause a pile of candy, chocolates, glitter, and noisy doodads to fly out from the corpse. This inspires all nearby allies within 30 ft as if they were given a Bardic Inspiration."},{"n": "Spellcleaver","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Battleaxe is infused with power by the presence of magic. When the wielder casts a non-cantrip spell the Axe becomes infused with energy adding an additional 1d4 force damage per spell level on the next attack made within 1 minute (this effect does not stack). The wielder may choose to replace force damage with the damage type of the spell that triggers it. '"},{"n": "Mirageblade","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Scimitar is invisible except for the hilt and guard. It grants advantage on attack rolls against opponents who haven't seen the weapon before or been hit by it."},{"n": "Flail of Arcane Vampirism","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Flail when striking an enemy can steal the magic from an enemies magic item rendering it ineffective for 1 minute (DC 15 Wis to resist). Once per day the Flail on a successful drain steal the magic of the item, gaining its effect for the flail's wielder for the next 24 hours."},{"n": "Wilting Flower","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Whip is a deep green and smells faintly of pollen with it's leather guard flaps resembling drooping flowerpetals. If this weapon strikes an enemy it may break off wrapping around an enemy weapon forcing them to make a Constitution Save DC 14 or wilt and flop over. Even metal or stone weapons soften and flop. This causes them to deal half damage for a full day. After using this effect the whip at that point ceases to function until the next dawn."},{"n": "Arm of God","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This magical arm can only be equipped to a creature missing one. It is a +3 weapon and grants the user 22 Strength with that arm only. It can be used an unarmed weapon dealing 1d8 damage. Additionally, once per day it may make 5 unarmed attacks as a single action."},{"n": "Omniglaive","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +2 Glaive is blocky and angular. Each successful melee attack adds a charge to this weapon (max 9). You may make a full round attack spending all the charges making an attack and gaining an additional attack at any enemy within 15 feet of the target per charge spent. Charges fade after 1 minute of not landing an attack. Using this causes one level of exhaustion to the user."},{"n": "Greatsword of Glass","r": "","t": "Weapon","u": "","d": "This +1 Greatsword deals 4d6 damage instead of the usual 2d6. Each time it hits an enemy this value is reduced by 1d6 until the blade snaps entirely and is useless. It regains 2d6 damage at dawn. Each strike creates a shower of glass shards, blasting creatures in a 15ft cone forcing a dex save to all creatures (DC12) or suffer 2d6 damage."},{"n": "Torvald's Brain Jar","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "1/day","d": "A jar filled with a light blue embalming fluid with small swirls of black ink. When a brain is placed inside the jar and the command word is spoken the jar will create an image in the jar depicting a scene in ink of the last 30 seconds of the creatures death. The scene loops until the command word is spoken again. The brain can be replaced once per day."},{"n": "Globe of Goblin Insight","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "1/day","d": "A bone globe with a corked top and filled with liquid and a bone with a rune word floats inside, when the command word is spoken and the globe is shaken. It gives a 1 or 2 word response as a Divination Spell, except the answer is given as if it were given by an Int 9 Goblin"},{"n": "Malleable Ingot","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A double length iron ingot. If the command word is spoken the metal can be rolled in your hands as easily as if it were being shaped in a forge and can be quickly moved into into any shape. This can be a small shield, weapon, or other object of similar size. Reforging takes a full round and can be done any number of times."},{"n": "Arsonist's Torch","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When activated the torch erupts in flame for 10 minutes. Each round all flammable objects within 5 feet catch fire. If it touches a living creature that creature must make a DC 10 Dexterity Saving throw or catch fire. If the torch is quenched or extinguished the effect ends immediately."},{"n": "Shadow Torch","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When lit the Shadow Torch emits a soft dark light as a torch, perfect for low light vision. Despite shedding light as a regular torch creatures further than 10 feet from the holder cannot see any of the light"},{"n": "Twinevine","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "Twinevine is a 50 foot length of vine ending in a bulb that functions as a rope. Due to it's rough grip and uneven surface checks made to climb it are granted +2. Additionally, if the end of the rope is cut it will regrow immediately to it's full length. No more than 50 feet of rope may be cut from the bulb per day. The cut rope will decay and crumble after a week."},{"n": "Manacles of Honorable Combat","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "The user can make an unarmed attack to try and clasp the manacles to an enemy that has arms. Once the manacles connect to two opponents each opponent gains advantage on all attack rolls against their connected opponent and disadvantage when attacking any other enemy. If one of the combatants spends their action to try and escape a DC15 Strength or Dexterity saving throw will let them escape the manacles."},{"n": "Glow Torch","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When lit the torch appears to shed a soft green light but no light is actually created. Instead living creatures within 15 feet light up as if Faerie fire had been cast on them."},{"n": "(Language) Bifocals","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When using the far lenses the wielder may read a book or text from up to 30 feet away. When less than 2 feet away from any writing they can read it as though it were common. This does not give the ability to read things written in code or otherwise disguised though."},{"n": "Charming Monocle","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "3 Charges","d": "A monocle with a pink lens and a silver frame. When the user spends their action and wink at an enemy that can see them within 30 feet, it spends 1 Charge to cast Charm Person (Wisdom DC 12) or 3 Charges to cast Charm Monster (Wisdom DC 14). If the enemy passes their saving throw the monocles then cast the same spell in reverse against the owner. It regains 1 Charge per day."},{"n": "Onyx Pendant","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When concentrated and held the pendant will vibrate if Undead are within 30 ft."},{"n": "Badge of Authority","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "Can cast disguise self at will, as a generic local member of authority - such as a guard. The Investigation check is DC13 to reveal it as an illusion"},{"n": "Goblin Sniffer","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A long crooked wooden goblin nose on a string. Once attuned the user gains advantage on perception checks involving smell or on skill checks involving Goblins. While normally Goblin, nose this comes in many other varieties such as Giant, Orc, Gnome, Kobold, etc"},{"n": "Prismatic Goggles","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "5 Charges","d": "Can fire Chaos Bolts out of the eyes of the goggles for 1 charge per Spell Level (Max 3 per cast). The elemental damage isn't random. They fire in order starting at a random number when the goggles are found. The goggles gain 1 charge a day."},{"n": "Bangle of Invisibility","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When activated the attached limb (and just the limb) becomes invisible as the invisibility spell."},{"n": "Bowtie of Swagger","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "The user can make a performance check as an action (DC 8) to gain the benefit of the Blur spell. The dance may be continued as a bonus action in subsequent rounds with the DC increasing by 3 each round."},{"n": "Oak Beehive","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A wooden beehive with a tiny tap on front. The Beehive can produce 1 flask of honey or mead a day. Once a day it can also be opened to summon a swarm of bees under your control as the Conjure animals spell. If dropped it will automatically activate 1d4+1 swarms with the bees targeting the closest unit and goes inert for a week."},{"n": "Hexbag","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A small pouch filled with bits of teeth and dried nightshade petals. When worn or held by anyone other than the owner anyone who attacks them gains the benefit as if the spell Hex was cast on the holder. The holder can make an investigation check (DC12) to locate and reveal the bag as an action after suffering damage from the effect. Ownership may be transferred during a long rest when the command word is spoken."},{"n": "Malekin's Magnificent Egg","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "1 Use","d": "A large white egg. When the command word is spoken and the blood or remains are sprinkled on top of the egg it will hatch into a Tiny version of the base creature provided. It has none of the supernatural or spell like abilities of the original."},{"n": "Boots of Animal Tracks","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This pair of fine boots is covered in multiple pieces of fur from different animals. The boots can be activated to leave tracks as if they were from any chosen animal."},{"n": "Lamp of Distraction","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When lit the colors and movement of the lamp mesmerized all nearby creatures who watch it. They must pass a DC11 Wisdom save or fall under the effects of the Enthrall Spell"},{"n": "Pillow of Wonderful Dreams","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When slept on the user can rest in half the time of a standard Long Rest. Additionally the DM rolls a d20 - on a 15+ they receive visions of the possible future and may be given story hints (DMs discretion), on a 12-14 the players sleep is filled with nightmares and on a 1-2 the DM may feed them false info or prophecies."},{"n": "Boots of Reversed Momentum","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "3 Charges","d": "If the user has moved more than 5 feet they may spend a charge to active the boots as a bonus action. This launches them 30 feet in the opposite direction last moved. Gain 1d3 charges per day."},{"n": "Magnetic Boots","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These heavy iron boots can be commanded to 'lock'. When 'Locked' the player is unable to move or be moved while active. Any creature may make a Strength check (DC18) to break the 'lock'. Once broken the boots cannot be activated for one week."},{"n": "Gloves of Greed","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These silk gloves are woven with interlaced golden thread with large glass crystals in the palms. They grant advantage on Sleight of Hand checks when taking things. When extended and activated as an action, all coins and small gemstones in a 15 foot cone fly into the users palm. Characters holding coin purses or gems are allowed to make a DC10 Dexterity Check to stop their possessions from getting pulled"},{"n": "Cloak of Beetles","r": "Rare","t": "Wondrous","u": "5 Charges","d": "Resistance Poison, Can spend 1 charge to turn into a swarm of insects (beetles) for 1 minute as an Action, you may also change back early as an Action. Regains d3 charges each day."},{"n": "Torch of the Abyss","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When lit this torch sheds Darkness as the spell instead of Light. If wielded the user is unaffected by this spell."},{"n": "Tag of Recall","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A thin metal chain with a metal tag on the end. When attached to an item that can be held in your hands and the owner speaks the command word and a time limit (Max 1 hour). After the time has elapsed the item teleports immediately to the owner's hand. This effect is usable once per day per item."},{"n": "Ladle of the Frosted Peak","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A large deep blue metal curved spoon created as a gift for a marauding Frost Giant King to always keep the taste of the north with him. It freezes any liquid inside the scoop in a single round. After being slain it was scavenged by a group of halflings who used it to freeze scoops of sugar'd milk as a delicacy. It was later used in combat by Slingers who used it to scoop from a well to create impromptu frozen slingstones."},{"n": "Robe of the Moon","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "5 Charges","d": "This Robe offers +1 to all saving throws and changes its phase each night and regains 1d3 charges. From Full to Waning to Dark to Waxing and grants different bonuses. More powerful versions of this robe may contain more maximum charges. Full: As a full round action you may teleport anywhere you can see up to 50ft per charge spent. Waxing/Waning: Gain Darkvision 30ft. As a bonus action can teleport where you can see up to 10ft per charge spent. Dark: Gain Darkvision 60ft. As a bonus action can turn invisible until the end of your next turn and teleport to a location you can see up to 5 ft per charge spent."},{"n": "Oven Gloves","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A mage with a sense of humor created these powerful black and red gloves. Anything placed inside takes 3d6 fire damage a round as it is heated intensely. When turned inside out they offer Fire Resistance to the wearer."},{"n": "Performers Mask","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A simple theater wooden mask with a clear expression carved and painted onto the face. While generally found by themselves, any number of these masks be worn at one time and they fuse into one another - they are also attuned as a set. A bonus action and a wave of your hand over the face allows you to shift which mask is active. Each mask has a different expression and can cast Command with a specific command once per rest - (DC 11 + 1 per mask). Mask of Joy +2 Persuasion, Command (Approach) Mask Sadness +2 Insight, Command (Grovel) Mask of the Stoic +2 Perception, Command (Halt) Mask of Anger +2 Intimidate, Command (Flee) Mask of Trickery +2 Deception, Command (Give)"},{"n": "Robe of Scrolls","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "3 Charges","d": "This robe is fashioned from scrolls fashioned together to appear like cloth with long sleeves that drop down into a readily available spot for reading. As a bonus action the chosen scroll slides and shifts into place on the sleeve to be read. The following scrolls are on the robe. Once all the scrolls have been cast the robe takes a week to recover all the scrolls. 1st Level Spells: Silent Image, Alarm, Detect Magic, Comprehend Languages, Jump, Sleep 2nd Level Spells: Find Traps, Darkvision, Gust of Wind, Magic Weapon, Bless 3rd Level Spells: Plant Growth, Dispel Magic, Meld into Stone, Nondetection"},{"n": "Bearded Helmet","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This furry helmet was crafted by Dwarves and given to their favorite emissaries of other races. It made them immediately at home in Dwarven lands, but sometimes after years of wearing one made them actually believe they were a dwarf all along. When worn the user grows facial hair at an astonishing pace creating a full luscious beard in a matter of days. Once the beard is fully grown and as long as it isn't shaved they gain the ability to read and speak Dwarvish, Gain +1 Constitution (Max of 20), have advantage against saving throws against poison and resistance to poison damage, and gain darkvision 30 ft."},{"n": "Bracers of the Wolf","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These modified bracers of defense (+2 AC when wearing no armor or shield), Once per day these can be used to summon two wolves to your aid for 10 minutes. These wolves will act in your defense"},{"n": "Demon Eyes","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These goggles are made of stone and corrupted by a Great Fiend. They allow their user to see through any illusions or disguises created by celestials or fey. Additionally the user gain Darkvision 30 ft and +2 to hit and damage against celestials with attacks and spells"},{"n": "Angel Eyes","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These goggles are made of stone and blessed by a Great Celestial. They allow their user to see through any illusions or disguises created by fiends or fey. Additionally the user gain Darkvision 30 ft and +2 to hit and damage against fiends with attacks and spells"},{"n": "Belt of Quickdraw","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This belt grants the user +2 to initiative and let's them draw a weapon once per round as a free action."},{"n": "Belt of Extreme Size Differential","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "While worn you appear to be ~2 inches taller than normal. Nearby medium or larger creatures within 30 ft are ~2 inches shorter than they normally are. This belt can cast Enlarge on yourself. When cast it also casts Reduce all on units within 30 feet (DC14 save). This can be used once per short rest."},{"n": "Bodybag","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large bag drips lightly with blood and ichor. It functions as a bag of holding but may only carry corpses and their direct possessions. It has space for 12 medium or smaller creatures. Large creatures count as 4 smaller creatures. While the bodies are in the bag they will not decay and remain perfectly preserved."},{"n": "Paint of the Beast","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical warpaint can be painted onto your face to mimic the tribal markings of an animal. The paint lasts for up to an hour. While painted you can speak with animals of the chosen type and gain Keen Sight, Smell, or Hearing based on what makes sense with the chosen animal. Once during its duration you may Cast Animal Friendship on the chosen animals. Once per animal maximum."},{"n": "Collar of Tiny Reanimation","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "Created by a powerful Lich who missed his dog when he transformed created this to keep them together for eternity. When this collar is placed on an animal or monstrosity of Small or smaller size it reanimates it as per the Animate Dead spell with unlimited duration. If the collar is removed or the creation is slain the collar becomes inert for 1d3 days but may be used on the same creature."},{"n": "Steelgrate Gills","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This this steel choker allows the wielder to breath in any liquid for up to 1 hour a day."},{"n": "Stocking of Stretching","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These long black socks are incredibly comfortable and appear to conform to the users unique foot and leg shape. Once on the user may stretch their feet and calves individually or as a pair up to 5 feet at will. This ability grants the user +5 bonus on all Athletics checks when climbing or jumping."},{"n": "Lover's Earrings","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These beautiful golden earrings feature a ruby shaped as half of a heart. When two people wear each half of the ring they may communicate back and forth as though using the message spell at will, only V components are needed for this ability."},{"n": "Guardian's Bandages","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These cloth handwraps can once per day be used to reach out within 30 feet and pull an unconscious unit to the user immediately stabilizing them. They are immobilized for 1 round but recover 2d4 hit points on their turn."},{"n": "Dominator's Bandages","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These cloth hand wraps can once per day be used once on a creature within 30 feet. They must make a DC 14 Dexterity check or become immobilized, a DC 14 Strength check or get pulled to the caster, and a DC 14 Constitution save or suffer 3d6 bludgeoning damage from being constricted."},{"n": "Riftwalk Greaves","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "10 Charges","d": "As a move action you may spend a charge to have these dark purple metal greaves teleport the user up to 30 feet to a location you can see adjacent to an enemy and make an immediate unarmed kick attack against an adjacent unit dealing an additional +1d4 force damage per charge expended. This item gains 1d4 charges at dawn. Each cast in the same combat costs an additional +1 charge."},{"n": "Infernal Dino Guardian","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small black and red stuffed dinosaur has eyes that glow with an internal fire. When thrown and a command word is spoken as an action, the toy turns into a full sized Allosaurus. This Allosaurus has immunity to fire and adds an additional 1d4 fire damage to all attacks. It may also also cast Firebolt at will from its mouth. Once slain, this object remains inert for one week."},{"n": "Mark of Combustion","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This deep red metal token has a symbol of a flame and two interlocked pieces. It remains inert until the inner portion is spun 180 degrees. One minute later it explodes dealing 6d8 fire damage to all creatures within 10 feet (DC 13 Dexterity Save for half damage). A creature unaware of the Mark gets disadvantage on it's saving throw."},{"n": "Mark of Vines","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This green wooden token is inscribed with the symbol of a seed. When scratched 1 minute later vines will spring from the mark and grab the creature or object in the tile it's on. If no creature is present it will attempt to grab the nearest creature as a Grasping Vine spell before activating. The targeted creature must make a DC 14 Strength check or become grappled and take 2d8 damage a turn for 1 minute. As an action the creature may make another saving throw. If successful they break from of the effect. A creature unaware of the mark has disadvantage on the initial save."},{"n": "Mark of Teleportation","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This pure white ivory token is inscribed with the symbol of a gate with a sliding gate. When the gate is lifted, 1 minute later the creature or object in it's same tile are teleported to a random location 300ft away, that is pathable and touching the ground unless a DC 14 Intelligence Save is made. A creature unaware of the mark has disadvantage on this save."},{"n": "Tiny Iron Mark-et","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small iron box has a slot for coins in the top. Once per week the user may insert 500 gold worth of coins which vanish upon entering the object. 1 minute later a mark will emerge from the coin slot. This will randomly be a Mark of Combustion, Vines, Thievery, or Teleportation"},{"n": "Mark of Thievery","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small pair of an interlocking platinum and copper coins have an icon of a purse and a hand respectively. When pulled apart 1 minute later the platinum coin teleports all possessions of the creature or object in its tile except the platinum coin, to the location of the copper coin unless a DC 14 Charisma save is made. A creature unaware of the mark has disadvantage on the save."},{"n": "Prismatic Torch","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This torch is slightly smaller than a typical torch. When activated it emits a soft light that is the color of the user's choosing. As an action once per day the torch may be activated to create a blinding sparkling colored light shooting 30 feet around the user. All creatures in the area must make a DC13 Constitution saving throw or be blinded for 1d3+1 rounds. Creatures who are aware of the impending effect gain advantage on this save."},{"n": "Bardic Journal","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This journal when read will display a small illusion of the scene being described over the book itself. The illusions evolves and shifts as the story does but does so using the readers inner imagination of what is happening so any details are left up to mimic the imagination of the reader."},{"n": "Mark of Dangerous Flight","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This light silver coin has three parallel wavy lines cut out of the center resembling the symbol for wind. When flipped at least three rotations it'll activate. One minute later all objects on the tile this coin is on are launched 80 feet into the air DC 13 Strength Save for (for half). A creature unaware of the mark has disadvantage on the initial save."},{"n": "Amulet of Banishment","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This brilliant gold amulet when attuned glows with an inner light. The weapon gains +1 to attack and spell rolls made against Fiends, Celestials, and Elementals. A cleric may also use their Turn Undead ability vs those enemy types."},{"n": "Arcane Fragmenter","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This is a \"tiny\" diamond shaped crystal. As an action while held the crystal may be teleported up to 30 feet to a location you can see. It floats there remaining still while active but may be attacked, it has an AC of 15 and 20 HP. It slain it falls to the ground remaining innert for 1d6 days. This item is immune to all spell effects and non-physical damage. Any Sorcerer or Wizard spells that affect a single target may instead effect any number of enemies within 15 feet of the crystal."},{"n": "Portable Window","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "If placed on a surface no thicker than 3 feet wide and the command word is spoken the window aheres itself to the wall and you can see through the window as if it were glass all the way through. Creatures on the other side cannot see back however. Additionally, once per week the window may be opened once attached and Creatures may move through the window to the other side of the wall."},{"n": "Stunning Robe","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magic robe when worn adds +1 to any spell saves. Additionally once per day if the user yells their Verbal component of a spell additionally adds 1 round of Stun to any spell effect that an enemy fails to save against."},{"n": "Comet of Ruin","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This glowing magic rock when activated orbits the user 5 feet away in cardinal directions moving 2 Tiles clockwise around the user. It will attack any creature or object that is in that square at the end of the users turn and uses the Owners SpellAttack for the attack roll and it deals 2d6 force damage on hit."},{"n": "Blanket of Slumber","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A creature resting under this blanket can do a long rest in 4 hours instead of 8 hours. Additionally when placed over an unwilling creature they must make a will save )DC11) as if affected by a Sleep Spell."},{"n": "Merfolk Girdle","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A creature wearing the merfolk girdle has their legs transform into a finned tail when submerged in water. Granting them a swim speed of 30 ft and the ability to breath underwater. Additionally, once per day they may activate the belt to create a cube of water 30 feet wide anywhere where they are present within the area. This effect lasts 1 minute, or until the user leaves the water."},{"n": "Bandana of Cowardice","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This black and gold bandana with the symbol of a fanged skull turns to pure white and flaps rapidly in the air when activated. The user becomes Frightened from all hostile creatures but gains an additional +15 speed, advantage on all athletic checks, and does not provoke attacks of opportunity from movement. The user may attempt a Charisma Save (DC 15) to end this effect at the end of each round. The Bandana can be activated once per hour."},{"n": "Skeleton Key of Ownership","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This Skeleton Key grants advantage on any checks to open or unlock doors. While inside a location any creature that spots you must make a DC13 Charisma Save or believe that you are in fact the proper owner of the establishment."},{"n": "Rat Tail","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical rat tail will occasionally twitch in response to danger or the presence of large creatures. When placed over where a tail would be on a tailless creature it will morph into a rat. Unwilling creatures may make a Wisdom save DC11 to resist the effect and may attempt to save again at the end of each turn. The user can also speak with Rats while in Rat form"},{"n": "Flamespitter Mask","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This mask has the features of a small blue furred devil. When activated it breathes fire for 1 minute. At the end of your turn you fire a cone 10 feet in front of the user dealing 2d6 fire damage (save Dex DC 10 for half). This is usable once per short rest."},{"n": "Emerald Snugg","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These were crafted by an ambitious gnome adventurer party whose small frame and pension to find lots of copper coins spurred them to create a solution. The Emerald Snugg was their answer. It is a small construct in the shape of a very stout turtle with an Emerald in the center of it's back. They follow around the person who activates them but will try and sniff out coins from 100 ft away. If they smell a coin they will move towards it and try to eat it. When consumed these coins are lost and the Emerald on it's back grows slightly as their value is fused into the gemstone. Once it has consumed 100 gold worth of coins it will shed its central gemstone which is worth 100 gold. These Snuggs also come in Sapphire, Ruby, Diamond, Topaz, and other gem variants that often have varying value levels."},{"n": "Gloves of the Mime","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This set of thin white gloves allows you to create a wall of force-like effect except it can only be maintained by pushing your hands against the space and only creates a single 10 by 10 panel. The gloves may also be mimic pulling a creature or object towards the user within 30 feet. If they fail a Dex Save (DC 15) they are pulled 10 feet towards the user and are immobilized the enemy may retry this save each round. You may also mime climbing a ladder to move straight up or down with a Climb speed of 20 feet for up to 1 minute as long as you continue the action. You may also mime a wall in front of your body which creates a 10 ft by 10ft Wall of Force which breaks after absorbing 30 damage. Each of these effects may be used once per day."},{"n": "Farsight Crystal","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small crystal lens can be attached to any bow or crossbow. When looked through the lens enhances and magnifies anything the user is looking at. It makes the weapon a +1 weapon if it isn't already and when prone and using a full round action to make a single attack the ranges of the weapon are increased by 5 times. (ex- a longbow with this attack has 750/3000 range)"},{"n": "Inferno Cart","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This contraption is a compressed metal cart meant for riding with a small furnace on the bottom. It has only 2 wheels in the front and back with handles attached to the front to turn the front wheel to steer and a small lock box on the back for the storage of small goods which can be opened with the command word. The cart can be easily pulled when inactive but when activated it roars to life flames shooting from the wheels granting it's rider a movespeed for 70 feet and granting the user and mount the effects of the Fire Shield spell. Turning more than 10 feet in a single move requires a DC5 acrobatics check for each square moves beyond 10 feet, or the user wipes out taking 1d4 damage for each Tile turned landing prone and deactivating the machine. Each hour it is active the small central furnace needs to be fed 25 gold worth of coal, gems, or coins."},{"n": "Facial Razor","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This incredibly sharp straight razor can trim any beard or facial hair easily and cleanly with a single pass. When flipped around to the flat edge. Running it along an area of skin causes it to grow hair if possible. Each pass with this variant can add half an inch of hair."},{"n": "Tarrasque Paper","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These sheets of paper usually come in multiples are are highly desired by wizards for their spellbooks and scrolls. These sheets are impervious to all mundane damage. They cannot be cut, burned, or destroyed by non-magical sources."},{"n": "Harnait's Overnight Forest","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These acorns usually come in a large bag with several dozen acorns. When planted each makes around 15 square feet of forest that grows to full size over the course of 1 day. The forest grows twice as fast if it isn't actively watched, and the plants are native to the terrain (ex Cactuses in a desert, pine trees in the mountains)"},{"n": "Stonecutter's Handbook","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This thin pamphlet contains the pictures, rituals, customs, secret language and symbols of a long dead organization. The book describes them as eternal and their practitioners swear that they are still powerful but operate entirely in secret. For one day after reading the handbook a reader understands and communicate messages with the Stonecutter's coded language, they also gain +1 to any skill checks involving stone. Comprehend languages and other such methods cannot understand this language. A reader may also pay 250 gold pieces and pray to the book and gain its benefits for 1 year without requiring continued reading. After 5 years of this practice this effect becomes permanent. Afterwords additional reader of this book later who pays will have a portion of their 250 gold magically appear in the hands, pocket, or coinpurse of that Stonecutter."},{"n": "Stormboard","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This pair of boots also comes complete with a narrow metal rectangle with curved edges. When the wearer places both their feet on the rectangle they lock into place and the board begins to hover. The user may levitate up 2 ft off the ground and gain an additional +10 speed and opponents making attacks of opportunity against them have disadvantage. Additionally they can benefit from the effects of Featherfall while active."},{"n": "Surgepack","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small copper box tingles when touched and can flare up with small surges of electricity. When attached to a metal weapon and attuned it adds 1d3 lightning damage on hit. When attached to a Stormboard it increases the levitate height to 5 feet and increases their speed by another +10. Additionally any time the user completes a movement where they leave an enemies threatened square they take 1d6 lightning damage (Dex save DC 12 for half)"},{"n": "Headband of Excessive Beauty","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "As long as long as the user's head and face is exposed this glorious headband grants the user +2 Charisma to a maximum of 18 and the ability to add their Charisma bonus to their Initiative roll and they are proficient in Intimidation, Persuasion, Performance, and Deception. Additionally, the wind is always seeming be glowing gently sweeping back their hair, even indoors. If the wearer has no hair a beautiful set of hair will grow within 6 hours. None of the benefits of the Headband will function until their hair is fully grown in."},{"n": "Paint of Wonder","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This gallon paint bucket if filled with water will become a multicolored paint overnight. The paint always appears to be a swirl of vibrant many colors. By speaking the out loud the desired color that paint will always leave the bucket the chosen color until a new color is chosen"},{"n": "Bonfire of Revival","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When lit as a full round action this magical bonfire rages for the next 10 minutes. It deals 2d6 fire damage to any creature standing in it's tile. If any creature within 100 ft is slain the user may use a bonus action to activate the bonfire. The user's body immediately catches flame and is reduced to ash. On their turn they emerge from the bonfire with 50% of their maximum health. This consumes the bonfire."},{"n": "Medallion of Eternal Glory","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This copper medallion is worn in a visible location. You also gain advantage on all Charisma checks against anybody wearing one of these medallions of a lower tier, but have a -2 penalty on all Cha Checks with anybody without a Medallion. The Medallion permanently upgrades when you assist in the slaying of an enemy of a specified CR or higher. Wood: +2 to Initiative, upgrades at CR2 Copper: +1 to all Saving Throws, upgrades at CR4 Silver: Immune to Frightened, upgrades at CR6 Gold: +1 to AC, upgrades at CR8 Platinum: Resistance to Fire and Cold, upgrades at CR10 Diamond: Can Reroll 1 Attack or Skill roll of your Choice once per Long Rest"},{"n": "Flutterwings","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small harness and rainbow butterfly wings can be used on any tiny or smaller animal granting them flight speed of 20. If attached to a familiar it also increases their Dexterity and Wisdom by 2."},{"n": "Handkerchief of Misery","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When offered to a creature they are overcome with intense sadness. They must pass a DC13 Charisma Save or begin to cry and weep uncontrollably forcing them to leave the situation. This automatically ends if the creature enters combat."},{"n": "Ponaise Disturbing Servant","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small frightening scarecrow is roughly 4 feet tall and covered in a dirty tattered black cloak. It's face covered in a mask with dark blood red eyes painted onto it and it has sickle's for hands. It is incapable of moving while anybody is watching it but it will immediately teleport behind the user if they leave more than 10 feet from it's presence and it remains unobserved. It can be commanded to fetch objects or perform basic tasks but will only complete them if it isn't being watched. These tasks are completed instantaneously if the Servant would have had enough time to complete them while unobserved. It may also appear behind other creatures of the owners choice, but again it must remain unobserved. Once per short rest it is allowed to make an melee attack with +5 to hit against an unaware enemy dealing 1d4+2d6 (sneak attack) damage. Additionally, the user can cast Fear (Wisdom DC13) once per day from the Servant's location granting disadvantage on the saving throw if the Servant is hidden from view."},{"n": "Extremely Absorbent Cloak","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This cloak is very comfortable and grants the user insulation and protection as if they always benefited from an Endure Elements spell. Additionally the cloak can absorb up to 100 gallons or 400 liters of liquid. When wrung out as an action as much of the liquid as the user wants is drained from the cloak."},{"n": "Scouts Eye","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This glass eye magically replaces the users eye (their choice) when attuned. It grants the user see twice as far with detail, and gain the ability to get advantage when saving vs illusions or spotting invisible creatures. It can be removed and thrown 100 feet into the air where it will hover and let the user look around from that vantage point for up to 10 minutes, this effect does not need to be continuous and it falls straight back down to the user when deactivated."},{"n": "Shock Choker","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "5 Charges","d": "This beautiful tight platinum necklace is studded with small topazes. It may be activated by the attuned Owner, which does not need to be the wearer. As long as the wearer is within 500 feet of the owner the necklace shocks the wearer for 2d8 lightning damage and spends 1 charge. They must also may make a saving throw Constitution DC14 or be stunned for 1 minute. Any creature reduced to 0 health by this damage automatically stabilizes. If the wearer attempts to remove the necklace without the owner's permission the necklace automatically activates. Removing this necklace requires a Sleight of Hand check DC 20. The wearer suffers disadvantage on this check. The necklace fully recharges at Dawn."},{"n": "Eyebrows of Excessive Expressiveness","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These eyebrows attune themselves to the user. When worn they move and adjust on their own to match the users mood and thoughts. While worn all intelligent creatures can understand the user regardless of language."},{"n": "Sash of Focus","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This sash grants the user unarmed attack damage of 1d4 if unarmored. If the user is a Monk they instead count as two levels higher for Ki Points and Martial Arts damage."},{"n": "Orb of Seasons","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This mystical orb when buried changes and effects the weather and surrounding plant and animal life within 1 mile. The owner may speak the command word to choose a season and the area responds accordingly. It may only be shifted once per day and takes 10 minutes to take full effect."},{"n": "JibJab's Instant Staircase","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This tiny brick staircase is only 2 inches tall. When activated it grows to become a fully complete brick staircase to a maximum size of 20 feet tall and long, though it may be stopped early. This stairwell never gains anything in terms of weight. If has AC 15 and 20 health. If it loses all it's health it reverts to its original size and cannot be reactivated for 1d4 days."},{"n": "Slowsand","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magic sand when thrown covers a 10 by 10 area. Any creatures in this area lose their next 1d4 turns unless they pass a DC 16 Will Save. They are unable to be interacted with in this state."},{"n": "Bracers of Incredible Confidence","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When worn these bracers grant proficiency to wield any weapon held. Additionally user finds themselves subconsciously and involuntarily doing flourishes and tricks with their weapons."},{"n": "Saltstick","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This +1 mace is made of forged crystal salts with the strength of steel. When striking an opponent they must make a Charisma save DC13 or suffer 1d4 psychic damage as salt stings and pours from their wounds. For the duration of the combat the first time each round they fail an attack or skill check they suffer an additional 1d4 psychic damage. This effect can stack any number of times."},{"n": "Tombstone of Eternal Remembrance","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical grave marker stands above a buried body or corpse. The tombstone may be asked up to 1d8 questions per day as if from a Spell With Dead spell, after which the spirit becomes irate and berrates the question asker. The answers appear as writing on the tombstone itself as if carved and remain until a new question is asked. Removing and reactivating the tombstone on a different body requires 100 gold worth of materials, mostly incense and preserved flowers, and a long rest present at the new body."},{"n": "Greedsbane","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large golden coin is cursed to punish those who are bound and driven by greed. If stolen or taken from its owner it will double the weight of all coins and currency held by the carrier each day (to a maximum of 50 lbs a coin). This effect lasts for a full month until removed."},{"n": "Flag of Incredibly Victory","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This flag has rallied armies from bitter defeat and turned many battles. It also has a powerful negative effect on morale and commanders would be wise to exercise caution of when and how they use this item. Once per day when raised this flag grants all allies who can see it within 60 feet the effect of the Aid and Bless spells for the next 10 minutes. The flag has an AC of 11 and 1 HP. Any ranged and spell attacks has disadvantage against it and it passes all saving throws. If destroyed it falls inert for 1 week and casts Bane on all Allies within 60 feet instead."},{"n": "Chest of Glorious Battle","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical chest when opened can pull inside up to 6 creatures. While inside the chest time is stopped in the outside world. Each creature rolls initiative and selects a role below and enters a 60 square foot pocket dimension that resembles an arena teeming with spectators and spawn equidistant from each other. All characters have 10 in all stats unless specifically mentioned. Wizard - Intelligence 14, HP 8, 1 cast of each - Mirror Image, Magic Missile, Silent Image, Thunderwave Fighter - Strength 14, HP 16, Throwing Axe, BattleAxe, Shield, Chainmail, Potion of Healing Rogue - Dexterity 14, HP 12, Daggers x4, Sneak Attack +1d6, Potion of Invisibility Cleric - Wisdom 14, HP 10, Mace, Shield, Chainvest, 1 cast of each - Cure Light, Command, Bless Ranger - Dexterity 14, HP 14, Short Sword x2, Short Bow, 6 arrows. Leather Armor, Hawk Pet. Monk - Strength 12, Dexterity 12, HP 10, Quarterstaff. Potion of Speed The losing side suffers 12d6 psychic damage if they face one enemy, 6d6 is two enemies, 3d6 if 3 enemies. 2d6 if 4 enemies, and 1d6 if 5 enemies"},{"n": "Toxin Mask","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This green mouth cover drips with vile and disease. While attuned the user is immune to the effect of being poisoned and has resistance against poison damage. While poisoned the user may spit poison as an attack with a range of 20 feet for 2d4 poison damage (Con Save DC 11 or become poisoned)"},{"n": "Irresistible Spices","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This delicious blend of rosemary, thyme, and cumin makes any food it is sprinkled on incredibly delicious and even alters it's cooking temperature up or down to match the consumers palette. It can be used to augment 2d6 meals or used on a single creature with an attack roll (without proficiency). If this delicious blend is applied to a creature they take 1d4 fire damage as the spices cook and sink into their flesh. All creatures within 30 feet must make a Wisdom Save (DC 12) or be compelled to charge and consume the individual. They may attempt to make another save at the end of each round. Affected creatures will use any claw or bite attacks available to them. If they have none they will use a bite attack that deals 1d3+Strength damage."},{"n": "Skull of Servitude","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "Up to 10 Charges","d": "This human skull has been dipped and infused with quicksilver. When placed on a Large or smaller body without a head the body will rise and serve the wielder with basic instructions. This creature functions as a Zombie of the appropriate size, and may retain some abilities of the former creature. (DMs discretion) The skull can be removed at any time, but if the zombie is slain the skull loses 1 of it's charges. When it runs out of charges it crumbles into silver dust."},{"n": "Accordian of Discomfort","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical accordion increases the DC of bard spells that require saving throws by 1. Additionally it may attempt to make a unit within 30 ft exceptionally itchy. If they fail their Charisma Save (DC13) they must try to remove their armor and weapons if they hold any."},{"n": "Slippers and Tassels of Epic Dancing","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical set of tassels and soft shoes are the tools of amazing interpretive dancers. They allow Bards specially trained in the art of dance and who are attuned to use their bardic inspiration and effect creatures with 2nd level spells and below without using Somatic components as long as the subjects of the effects can see them perform."},{"n": "Flute of Inspiration","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This flute augments and empowers Bardic Inspiration when used. If attuned and used by a Bard it increases the die of their bardic inspiration (up to a d12). If used by a non-bard they gain proficiency in Performance and may use Bardic Inspiration once per day as a level 1 bard."},{"n": "Bagpipes of Distraction","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This powerful set of bagpipes increases the number of times a bard can use Bardic Inspiration by 1 per day. Additionally, Bardic inspiration may instead be used as Bardic Distraction and may be used on hostile creatures to penalize a roll by the amount instead of adding to it."},{"n": "Band of the Dance","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This thin silver headband has a marble opal in the center. As the user spins and dances it begins to glow increasing in brightness. The user is allowed to make a DC 15 Performance check with an amazing dance. If successful they benefit from the full proficiency bonus when using Jack of All trades."},{"n": "Augmented Armbelt","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large grasping arm is attached to a girdle wrapped around the user waist. It moves as if it is the owner's own flesh and blood. It can hold things, use skill checks etc. Additionally, if it wields a weapon it can make a free attack with what it's holding ,when you make an attack action."},{"n": "Cowl of Silence","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical face covering grants the user +2 to stealth checks. Additionally when making a sneaking or hiding check all allies within 10 feet may opt to use their check instead of their own."},{"n": "Amulet of the Warmaster","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This amulet once attuned grants a Battlemaster the ability to increase their d8 superiority dice to d10s. Additionally once each rest they may replace one of their active maneuvers with a different one."},{"n": "Boots of Water Mastery","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "5 Charges","d": "These thin boots grant the user the ability to walk on water. Additionally they may be activate for 1 charge each to achieve any of the following effects as a bonus action at the cost of 1 charge. Flood - Water rushes from the boots covering the area within 20 feet of the user in several inches of water. This water will not outside the area it was created in. Steam - All creatures within 20 feet who are touching a liquid surface get scalded at steam erupts from the ground. This deals 2d8 fire damage (Dex Save DC 12 for half) Freeze - All creatures within 20 feet who are touching a liquid surface are frozen in place as the ice clings to their feet. They suffer 1d4 frost damage and are immobilized (Str Save DC 12 to avoid immobilize). This save may be attempted each round until success."},{"n": "Crown of Knowledge's Burden","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical circle gives the user the ability to read any language and advantage on any checks to read or decipher coded/ secret languages. Despite its power and usefulness it was used to murder the great Archmage Gizmo when it was delivered to him in the central library. When worn all nearby unread books fly to the user which can be easily caught with an open hand, but any books beyond that deal 1d3 bludgeoning damage as they viciously strike the user desperate to be read. If attended they may get a saving throw (DC 12 Strength) to resist this effect. Additionally the user can read an entire book in a single round but suffers 1d2 psychic damage when using this ability."},{"n": "Scabbard of Flames","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical scabbard can attune itself to any sword. When drawn sparks streak across the blade as it emerges dripping with oil. These sparks ignite the oil covering the blade in thick flames for 1 minute. These flames add +1d4 fire damage to all attacks with an additional 1d4 lightning damage on the first turn it is drawn. This can be used once per short rest."},{"n": "Shawl of Doves","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "3 Charges","d": "This soft white feather shawl is incredibly comfortable and grants +1 to all saves. Additionally you gain advantage on all persuasion checks as Doves fly from the wearer whenever they enter a new room. Once per day you may attempt to blind an enemy in melee with doves (Con DC 13)."},{"n": "Siphoning Manacles","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These manacles when clasped between two creatures steal health from the right manacle and pass it to the creature possessing the left manacle. The manacles siphon at a rate of 1 health per minute."},{"n": "Supporting Structure","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small padded stool when attuned will follow behind the user a short distance. When any creature including the owner falls, or is knocked prone the Stool will use it's reaction to fly under the creature and soften it's fall as if using a Feather Fall spell, or prevent the creature from being knocked prone."},{"n": "Weapon of Mass Destruction","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This powerful weapon (typically a Warhammer or Maul) has a +2 Modifier. However critical hits from this weapon deal an additional 1d8 damage and knock an enemy back 10 ft. Additionally, this weapon deals 3x damage to inanimate objects."},{"n": "Augmentation Kit","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This craftsman's kit contains all manner of hooks, widgets, and materials that may be used to modify up to 3 weapons by adding Light, Finesse, Reach, Throwing (20/60), Versatile, or change it's damage to Slashing/Piercing/Bludgeoning. A weapon may only have one of these attributes added. Additional uses replace the existing modifier. These can be used to augment Magical Weapons, Artifacts though are too durable and powerful to modify."},{"n": "Blowgun","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This +1 Blowgun contains the power of wind. It doubles the range of the Blowgun and can cast Gust of Wind whenever you make an attack. This is usable one per minute."},{"n": "Super Fungi","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small dehydrated mushroom activates when it's hydrated comes to life as a 5ft tool mushroom person for the next hour. This mushroom person is incredibly fun and charismatic with 4Hp, 6 in all stats and 18 Charisma and +8 to Performance (Dance checks). It can perform simple tasks for you, seeks to high fives as much as it can, and will help creature that asks it to the best of its ability. After it's duration expires or it is slain the mushroom person takes a long rest to recharge, or a short rest if it was hydrated with alcohol."},{"n": "Shimmercloak","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This beautiful cloak absorbs and distorts nearby colors drawing in the gazes of nearby viewers. The user may cast invisibility on any creature within 5 feet and remain invisible as long as they stay adjacent to the wearer."},{"n": "Medallion of Impeccable Courage","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This medallion was crafted for halfling rangers responsible for tracking down and killing giants. This user is immune to being frightened. Additionally they gain +1 to attack rolls for each size larger their target is and -1 to attack rolls for each size smaller."},{"n": "Cloak of the Swamp Hag","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This cloak is dripping with mud and filth. It offers the wearer a swim speed of 15 feet through water or mud, and ignore terrain penalties for mud, sand, or gunk. Additionally, this can release a terrible stench causing all creatures within 20 feet to be stunned for 1 round (DC14 Con save to ignore). The user also gains minor illusion as a cantrip but can only make ugly things."},{"n": "Memory Bead","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A small glass bead created for the purposes of storing, transmitting, and retaining information. A skilled mage is allowed to transfer a memory of whomever they are touching and transfer it into the bead. When broken the user immediately gains the memory as if it were their own."},{"n": "Experience Bead","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "A variation on the Memory Bead, but instead of containing a memory the bead when broken grants the user the skills and craft experience of whatever expert crafted the bead. For 1 hour the user gains proficiency and a +4 bonus on any checks made of the appropriate skill."},{"n": "Shepard's Knapsack","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This knapsack gives the user the ability to cast Charm Animal (as Charm Person - DC 11) 3 tunes per rest. Additionally the knapsack can be opened to reveal a portal to a mini dimension much like a bag of holding. Unlike a bag of holding their is sufficient oxygen for creatures inside to survive for up to a week, and it's full of lush grasses and a small pond for drinking. The bag can hold up to a dozen animals, but will not allow non-animals to enter. The user can choose when and how to remove things simply by reaching inside."},{"n": "Nobberosh's Correction Apparatus","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "3 Charges","d": "This apparatus is worn around and under a set of armor. It's thin metal blades and rings lie close to the body and react when movement occurs. The user is generally more nimble than you might expect as the metal supports the natural body movement and offers resistance to allow it to turn and react quickly, which increases the Dexterity Modifier by 1, If the user is poisoned, the armor will immediately administer an anti-venom dealing 1d3 piercing damage. If the user is knocked prone, or forcefully moved the armor strikes back correcting the position dealing 1d3 bludgeoning damage and spends a charge. It regains it's charges each day. If the user is immobilized, charmed, or stunned the metal arms slap and painfully poke the user dealings 1d3 piercing damage giving them the chance to reroll the saving throw if applicable."},{"n": "Tanglefoot's Scrumptious Edibles","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These halfling made bakery sweets are hollow on the inside allowing them to be filled with delicious sugary filling. Any potion effect that lasts for 1 minute or more may be condensed into these sweets forming a baker's half dozen (7 edibles). These bonuses apply for only a single round but may be eaten as a bonus action as they are tiny and easy to pop into your mouth."},{"n": "Liquid Ink","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "While obviously most Inks are liquid these enchanted inks are used for colorful and magical tattoos. When applied that can shift shapes if the user spends a an action the tattoo will shift to a new shape over the next minute. It must be roughly the same amount of ink, but can change color."},{"n": "Buttery Mail","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This envelope has a small extra pouch attached to it. When a buttery treat is placed in the pouch and a letter inside the envelope it will fly from the holder's hand and seek out who the letter is addressed to. The buttery treat which will be consumed with a loud chewing sound as it takes flight. The envelope has an AC of 22 in flight and a Fly speed of 90. A few small additional objects may also fit inside the pouch."},{"n": "Brand of Communal Judgement","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This scalding branding iron is a 1 damage stick +1d4 fire damage that attack a creature where it burns into their flesh and marks them as cursed unless they pass a DC 13 Con Save. When cursed at the end of any social exchange with another creature interacts with the brand owner must ask how satisfying their interaction was on a scale of 1-5. The scores are cumulative and the average is rounded to the nearest point. At any point if the Brand owners average score falls below 5 they suffer 1 level of permanent exhaustion for each point below 5. If the Brand is used on a new target any marked creature has the mark removed, killing the owner of the Brand of Judgement or receiving a 5 point rating from the owner will also remove the effect."},{"n": "Wheels of Perpetual Motion","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These wheels come in sets of two. These can be applied with an action and may be concealed with a sleight of hand check. When applied the user can choose to have them be fixed direction or variable. Variable simply mimic and augment the users movement by sliding forward they move. They force the user to move forward 10 feet at the start of their turn. If fixed, instead they will always move the user 15 feet in the specified direction until removed (with a DC 14 Strength check) at the end of their turn."},{"n": "Iron Turtle","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small iron shelled turtle is a powerful defensive tool. It can be thrown to deflect an attack within 20 feet as a reaction subtracting 1d6 from the attack roll and being knocked 20 feet in the opposite direction of the attacker. It has a speed of 5 and will try to return to it's owner."},{"n": "Scrollwheel","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This bracer is worn as normal but has a spinable outer ring that can hold scrolls. Scrolls place here can be very quickly turned and read through. This device allows the reader to quickly scan and read multiple scrolls off in rapid succession allowing them to cast 2 spell scrolls as a single action."},{"n": "Wings of Knowledge","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "6 Charges","d": "This wings are made from lengths of scroll fused together. The wings we activated a charge is spent grant 10 minutes of flight with a flight speed of 10+ 5 feet per charge when cast. While active embers slow and chew through the available paper shrinking the size of the wings at roughly 1 foot of wingspan per charge. Scrolls, even ones already used, can be consumed to be add 1 charge to the wings"},{"n": "Feather of Authenticity","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large and colorful feather pen can write as normal. However it's main power is being able to consistantly sign the wielders name with perfect consistency. It can write in traditional ink or in magic ink. If written in magic ink it can write on any surface, and in any color(s), but the results can only be read with a Detect Magic spell where it glows brightly."},{"n": "Lantaro of Introduction","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This pure white small orb floats gently by the user granting them +1 Charisma. When a creature it has not interacted with before comes within 20 feet of the user it will fly over and glow gently but inform them of the owner, their title, their status, etc through telepathy. Each Sphere has a different personality that is very different from their maker - some are humble, some are threatening or braggarts, while others are comforting and excited. Their color and brightness changes as they communicate and their emotion changes. It has an AC of 10 and if struck will deactivate for an hour."},{"n": "Lantaro of Beratement","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This angry small red orb floats around the user granting them +1 Intelligence. It can be ordered to move and circle around a nearby foe within 30 feet as a bonus action. While circling an enemy it will insult them. Each sphere has a different personality, but all are witty and intelligent in their insults - some are cruel, some funny, and others are simply flippant and mocking. Whenever the creature they are circling fails an attack or skill check against the owner or the owner succeeds an attack or skill check against them they suffer 1 psychic damage as the little creature mocks them ruthlessly. It has an AC of 14 and if struck will deactivate for 1d4 rounds."},{"n": "Lantaro of Whispers","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This powerful dark tiny orb will circle the user granting them +1 Wisdom. It periodically flies around and investigates nearby objects and creatures whispering secrets, trivia, and legends, and rumors of what is investigating and switches languages every few sentences. Each sphere has a different personality based on it's maker - some are shy, others confident, and some uncertain or curious. Typically the information discussed is decypherable though the owner can ask it one question for each language the owner knows per day. The sphere is exceptionally smart and is usually very helpful, similar in power to a Commune spell, though the information provided is often heavily biased. It has an AC of 11 and if struck will deactivate for an hour."},{"n": "Lantaro of Life","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This twisting green tiny orb will circle the user granting them +1 Constitution. It loves to snuggle living creatures and has a special fondness for plants and tiny animals. It makes excited clicks and whistles which increase in frequency if it recieved well, but will flee in terror and silence itself if recieved poorly. Each sphere has a different personality based on its maker - some are touch heavy, others purr, and some simply focus more on humming or pulsing warmly. The first time it touches a wounded creature each day it restores 1 hp or automatically stabilize downed creatures. It will also seek out plants and flowers and make them bloom, twist, and grow more rapidly. It has an AC of 12 and if struck will deactivate for an hour."},{"n": "Lantaro of Flickering","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This tiny light blue orb floats around the user granting them +1 Dexterity. It circles the owner restly flickering in and out of existence, teleporting and bouncing around if it is forced to sit still but all are very quiet except for the noises made from their movement. Each sphere has a different personality based on its marker. Some prefer to zig and zag, others spin, and some prefer to sit very still but then rapidly teleport around in rapid inch long hops. It can teleport an adjacent willing creature 5 ft to another location it can see once per round. It has an AC of 15 and if struck will deactivate for an hour."},{"n": "Lantaro of Burden","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This hard shelled tiny yellow orb floats around the user granting them +1 Strength. It loves to lift things of varying shapes and sizes and will constantly try to pick things up, often accidently taking things it shouldn't in the process. While generally quiet or humming softly, the harder it works the brighter it glows and the louder it hums. It has a Strength score of 14. Each sphere has a different personality based on its maker. Some prefer to push or pull, some like to do lots of lighter reps, others try to show off the raw size of objects they can lift. Once per combat the owner may as a bonus action direct the orb to pick up an object or to attempt to grapple an enemy. It has an AC of 13 and if struck will deactivate for an hour."},{"n": "Mask of Words","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This mouth covering is covered in text and can be used to decieve and speak for others. If a creature within 30 feet fails a Charisma save (DC13) they are silenced, but you can speak for them with whatever words you want, in their voice. They are allowed an additional save at the end of their turn and once broken cannot be effected for 24 hours. An investigation check vs the users deception can spot the user whenever a save is made."},{"n": "Samuels Stupendous Suit","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This brightly colored and fashionable outfit radiates with style and nobility. It is enchanted to never stain or dirty under any circumstances."},{"n": "Halflings Scout Belt","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This belt is thick tweed belt smells faintly of cakes and tea. The owner can speak and read Halfling and their appetite is increased noticeably. When worn by a small creature it can be used to turn invisible for up to 10 minutes once per short rest. If worn by a medium or large creature it instead makes only their torso invisible."},{"n": "Stein of Endless Ale","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This ornate platnium stein is covered with beautiful ivory carvings of men and women drinking joyously in a tavern. When the top is closed and the words \"Another round of X for Y\" is yelled the Stein will magically be refilled with the desire liquor when the chosen person opens the Stein."},{"n": "Aquara Helm","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This helm has a glass visor and is filled with a recycling volume of water. It is primarily used by aquatic races who cannot breath air, but occasionally powerful mages have used it as a reliable fish bowl."},{"n": "Archbakers Infinidough","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This loaf of bread dough can pulled into multiple loaves each day. Additionally if the command word is spoken the bread rises and begins to expand and cook immediately gaining immense amounts of volume. It expands 5 feet per round in all directions for up to 10 rounds. Any creature in the way of the bread must make a DC14 Dex Save or get immobalized by the bread. They are allowed an additional save each round to break end the effect. Any creature trying to move through the bread moves at a speed of 5 and will suffocate as if underwater."},{"n": "Donut of Holding","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This enchanted donut is quite large for a donut and contains a secret pocket dimension similar to a bag of holding. The opening is the hole of the donut and only food items may be added or removed from the bag. It can hold a total of 20 cubic feet of food items and if the donut is consumed entirely all objects inside of it are lost forever. If the donut is only partially consumed it will return to it's full size at dawn."},{"n": "Muffin of Death","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small cursed Muffin is one of the most devastating items ever unleashed by the god of Death himself inspired by the effectiveness of Mimics. The muffin is incredibly tempting and upon being bitten into the biter must make a Con save (DC 13) or be turned into a muffin themselves for 1 hour. They have a movement speed of 5 in Muffin form. The Muffin of Devastation then comes alive with 30 hp, AC 14 and will attempt to consume the new muffin with bite attacks +7 w.1d10 damage. If slain, the cursed creature rises as a Muffin of Death. If the Muffin of Death is slain it returns to life in 24 hours unless completely destroyed."},{"n": "Shoes of Not-So Brave","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This pair of green magic shoes glow with power and pump the owner full of adrenaline as fear floods their system. They give the owner +10 speed when moving away from enemies. Additionally once per short rest any time the owner is attacked by a ranged attack or surprised they may spend a reaction to fall prone and attempt a hide check."},{"n": "Jellydonut of Infinite Filling","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This jellydonut when broken will spill jam. It begins with a trickle releasing a jar of jam a minute but can be activated to begin spraying gallons of jelly a minute. It can be aimed and will cover a 5 ft tile per round within 30 feet with jelly. Changing the aim or trajectory of the donut can be done as a bonus action. This tile becomes difficult terrain and any creature in it or walking through must make a Dex Save DC 11 or fall prone. This save difficulty increases by 2 for each round the donut sprays onto that tile. The donut may be deactivated where it hardens and becomes inedible for 24 hours. As a bonus action the user may change the flavor of jelly that emerges."},{"n": "Gloves and Sandals of Control","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This set of Gloves and Sandals each have a very small immovable rod inside. While not as powerful as a full sized rod, once attuned follow the will of the user and allow them to climb up or down at a speed of 15 feet. The trick is because each glove and sandal operates inpendently and two are sufficient to carry their weight they can climb up or down anywhere without needing walls or any support. This does functionally allow them to levitate or very awkwardly fly. As a reaction these can also be used to reduce the distance the wearer is pushed or pulled by 5 feet."},{"n": "Oxygen Pebble","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These bright white stones are incredibly light and almost float when held or tossed. When placed in wate for 1 hour they emit an immense amount of tiny oxygen bubbles. In a 10 foot cube around and the pebble any creature that breathes air can breath fine in the bubbles. Any creature that cannot breath air finds themselves unable to breath and begins suffocating."},{"n": "Cloak of the Deep Wilds","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This long green camoflauged cloak is covered in ornate pattern of thorns and brambles and the edges are laced with thorny vines. This cloak grants advantage on Stealth checks in the woods. Additionally as a bonus action the cloak can become a 5 ft bush around the user which they may attempt to hide in, or revert to cloak form. The bush causes the wearer to move at half speed and is removed if struck by a melee attack. Additionally, the may move through natural difficult terrain without penalty."},{"n": "Portal Potty","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This Enchanted Toilet seat was created by a Sorcerer who could not be bothered to clean her chamberpot. When 'used' it functions as a one-way portal to a location within one mile. A Ritual spell can be cast and 50 gold in incense and cleaning agent can be used to change the exit point of portal to where the spell is cast."},{"n": "Rogue's Haybale","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "These powerful items were designed by famous thieves and assassin guilds. This enchanted haybale can be bound and carried though it is heavy roughly 40 pounds. It can be opened and released as an action (rebinding takes a full minute). Any creature jumping into this haybale takes no fall damage. Additionally, if any creature hides inside the bale they gain advantage on their hide check."},{"n": "Wishseed","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small seed when planted it will sprout a tiny plant that animates and asks what the planter would like it to become. Whatever the planters ask it will become any plant or plantlike creature over the next 24 hours, it can even be a made up plant as long as it is well described to the seed. If it becomes an animated plantlike creature the Wishseed will be thankful to the planter for giving it life but it will not serve them and remains neutral. One month after the plant is born it will create a small green pod that contains another wishseed."},{"n": "Arthul's Frozen Throne","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This throne is crafted out of ice that never melts. When placed and the ritual is cast this throne creates a palace of ice around it that grows at a rate of 25 feet per day to a maximum of 150 feet in all directions with the exact specifications the ruler desires. If the throne is placed in a cold or frozen climate this extends to 1000 feet. The ruler also gains Immunity to Cold damage while in the palace and can use Frost Breath (60 ft cone - 8d8 cold damage DC16 Dex for 1/2 damage) 3 times per day."},{"n": "Torturer's Hooks","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This set of lockpicks also functions as a set of tortuerers tools with razor sharp edges and hooks. These instraments excel at delivering pain and offer advantage on any checks to torture information out of a creature. Once per day they can also function as a Zone of Truth while torturing a creature."},{"n": "Moneytree","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small enchanted clay pot has etchings of a platinum, gold, silver, and copper plants around the edges. If is filled with soil and a coin is planted beneath surface it will spout a plant that grows over the course of a week into a small tree. The tree grows fruit which are identical material coins to the one planted. It can grow 6d6 copper coins, 4d6 silver coins, or 2d6 gold coins, or 1d6 platinum coins. The original coin is consumed by the plant. The pot will not grow another tree until it is properly thanked and appreciated. The level of thanks needed goes up with the tier of tree grown."},{"n": "Wildred's Wonderful Wagon","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large covered wagon looks unassuming from the front. It's fairly small and can be pulled by a single horse or donkey if needed, and comfortably pulled with 2. Upon entering the wagon this 5x10 space is much large and more spacious than expected. Inside it's a 10x30 space complete with a two tents taking up 5ft each at the end for bedding or for storage. The atmosphere inside is kept just below room temperature and soft music plays echoing across the wagon, which can be turned on or off with an action. Covered lantern light covers the interior and a flap on the top can be opened when the weather is nice to get a breeze inside and bath the wagon in sunlight. This setup grants the users +2 to any diplomacy checks to buy, sell, or trade goods while inside. Even when moving the interior of the wagon stays completely still. When the user is attuned to the wagon if any uninvited guests enter the wagon an Alarm spell activates for the owner and any creatures they wish who have been inside the wagon in the last 24 hours."},{"n": "Mound of 1 Million Ants","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "When activated this clay mound can be placed or thrown up to 5 feet per point of Strength and Dexterity. On the following round it summons a Swarm of Insects (Ants). It summons another Swarm each round for the next 5 minutes or until destroyed. The Mound has AC of 12 and 25 Hp. These Swarms do not serve the summoner and will attack the closest non-Swarm unit each turn. These Swarms will aggressively guard the Mount and will not go beyond 30 feet of it. This Mound is usable once per day and will require a week to recharge if destroyed. Additionally, if the Mound is soaked in Honey, Sand, or Poison overnight the next time it is used it will summon Bees, Scarabs, or Spiders instead gaining Flight 30, AC 16, Regeneration 5, Poison Bite (as Bite but - DC12 Con or 2d6 poison damage)."},{"n": "Pendant of Water Repulsion","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This pendant is soft and pliable and feels like it's moving and flowing when held. When the commandment is spoken, the pendant creates a bubble of air that repels any liquid within 5 feet. This functionally lets the user walk as if the liquid didn't exist."},{"n": "Cloak of the Flapping Bird","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magic cloak is made of bright bold simple colors and is covered in feathers. It slows the rate of falling of the user to 10 feet a round and they fall in the same direction maintaining their speed. As a full round action the user may flap the wings of the cloak to change their rate of speed up to a maximum of their walking speed turn up to 90 degrees. Each time they flap they shoot up 25 feet in the air."},{"n": "Thinskin Compass","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This rodentskin compass is incredibly thin and soft to the touch. The arrow points to north, but if the user doesn't seem appreciative and offer thanks to the compass frequently the compass will actively try to mislead the user. Actively insulting or expressing frustation at the compass not doing its job will cause it to burn and scald the users hand. If it feels appreciated it will give the user advantage on any Survival checks about trying to the appropiate locations. If you are super complementary to the point of even offering gifts and immense thanks the compass will actively mislead the user but to purely positive results. It may lead the user to shortcuts or even secret locations."},{"n": "Recycler","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This backpack has green straps. When an object is placed inside and the bag is shaken the magic takes place. The object is decomposed into its component pieces and then falls out of the bag."},{"n": "Bell of Paranoia","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small bell will ring when an enemy is close. It has a +10 to hide checks, and if an unit moves to investigate it and remains hidden it will teleport up to 15 feet away."},{"n": "Bauble of Explosives","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This glass bauble when broken creates a box full of firecrackers and explosives. If lit it will begin firing rockets at random targets within 50 feet (as a Magic Missile spell), and explode violently after 1 minute as if a fireball was cast centered on it."},{"n": "Bauble of Light Inversion","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This glass bauble when broken reverses the lighting within 60 feet. Pitch darkness is changed to bright sunlight and sunlight turns to darkness. This effect lasts for 5 minutes, shrinking by 10 feet per minute afterwards."},{"n": "Accordian of Echoes","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "7 Charges","d": "This accordian grants +1 to DC of any Bard spells cast with it. Additionally, you may expend 1 charge per level of the spell (or 1 for cantrip) to have the spell be cast again automatically on the same target on the following turn. This instrument recharges 1d3 charges per day. This increases to 1d4+1 charges if two additional creatures and the wielder spend at least 15 minutes singing it a goodnight lulliby."},{"n": "Bauble of Cats","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small glass orb when broken releases 5d20 feral cats that spring out in all direciton."},{"n": "Bauble of Soup","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This glass bauble when broken creates a massive cauldron of boiling, simmering, soup. The soup can be delicious or disgusting (wielders choice), and can burn creatures for 3d4 fire damage per round if in the soup."},{"n": "Ancenstral Charm","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This ancient charm hangs from a necklace with a large bead of amber. When the ritual is performed the wielder summons the spirit of one of their ancestors from the beyond and binds them to the necklace. This ritual costs 50 gold and the ancestor is rarely pleased, but will begrudgingly help the wielder with whatever knowledge or expertise they possessed in life. The wielder can benefit as if proficient in a single skill the spirit would have known"},{"n": "Burden of Pain","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This heavy solid iron amulet is forged in the symbol of a weight with etching describing various sins and mistakes. This lowers the speed of the user by 10 but grants an additional 20 Temporary Health outside of combat. As a reaction once per day the wielder may activate the item until the start of their turn. On the wielders turn they manifest a large psychic weight over the head of a creature within 60 feet which comes crashing down dealing psychic damage equal to 2d6 + the amount of damage suffered during its activation (Dex Save DC 13 for half)"},{"n": "Helm of Extreme Bravery","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magic helm grants immunity to Frightened. Additionally the wielder gains +1 to all saving throws per enemy within 30 feet."},{"n": "Vest of Healing","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This tight but comfortable vest can be worn over armor. When attuned all incoming healing is increased by 1, + an additional 1d6 per spell level when healed."},{"n": "DoppleGolem","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "The Dopplegolem can be bound or trained to a single creature with a ritual spell that costs 100 gold. Once complete the Dopplegolem, while it cannot speak, takes on the personality and characteristics of the target. Additionally, the Dopplegolem gains the powers and effects of a level 1 version of that creature. If destroyed it can be rebuilt for 250 gold pieces."},{"n": "Door of Excessive Shutting","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magical wooden door is very difficult to close granting disadvantage on any attempts to open it or keep it open. Each time a creature passes through it, it will slam shut potentially dealing 1d4 bludgeoning damage in the process. If the door is destroyed it will reform within 1d4+1 rounds."},{"n": "Golemling","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small construct is the size of a small child. When activated a creature within 60 feet may be chosen as the Goleling's 'parent'. The Golemite will then proceed to follow the parent and cling to them (reduce speed by 10),if denied this honor it will try to pick up and break their stuff (Strength 10) or Flail (+4 Attack 1d2 damage). It has a speed of 20, an AC of 10 and 5 HP. If destroyed it reforms within 1d4+1 rounds. If it is unable to reach its parent in 24 hours it will become innert."},{"n": "Sporting Slingstaff","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "3 Charges","d": "This Quarterstaff can also has a sling attached. When activated as an action and a charge is spent the wielder specifies a number of rounds (Max 10). That many rounds later if the wielder hits an enemy with the sling they gain 1d4 bonus damage for each delayed. If the wielder uses the sling before that round -or- they reactivate the effect, the original bonus is lost."},{"n": "Pipe of Illusions","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magic pipe to allows the player to cast Major Image as will through smoking it. Only creatures that have smoked from a Pipe of Illusions within the last hour can see the images."},{"n": "Pauldrons of Feedback","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This set of Pauldrons grants the user +1 AC. Additionally each time a creature within 30 feet casts a spell they suffer 1d4 psychic damage, plus an additional 1d4 damage for each spell level."},{"n": "Slimplate","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This splint mail doesn't offer disadvantage on stealth checks, weighs only 20 pounds, and has a Dex Bonus of +1. It also makes the wearer look incredibly thin."},{"n": "Infernal Heart","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large demon heart infuses with the wielders flesh but remains partially exposed. It gives them the ability to speak infernal and abyssal and increases Constitution to 18. However, due to the exposed heart critical hits against the wearer deal 3x damage instead of 2x damage."},{"n": "Lightning Stone","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This powerful stone is a glass capsule with a lightning bolt captured inside. When placed next to a magic item it will infuse 1d4 charges into the item. This item recharges when struck by Lightning, a Lightning Bolt spell, or suffers 30 Lightning damage."},{"n": "Inciting Dummy","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This large wood and straw training dummy always appears to be taunting the enemy with a stupid inanimate grin. Any creature that is trying to attack or use an ability against the owner or their allies must make a Cha Save DC 14 or attack the dummy. The dummy has 20 health and AC of 15."},{"n": "Cloak of Images","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "Each time the user casts a spell an image appears (as Mirror Image) for each level of the spell. Each round one of these images will fade away."},{"n": "Sandals of Momentum","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This set of sandals has golden wings along the side. Each round the player takes the dash action they gain +5 speed to a maximum of +60 Speed. This effect is removed one round after they take a Dash action."},{"n": "Vision of the Dead, can only use while dead. can fly, invisibility, incorp, etc","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "The mask is one of a ghastly spectre. It allows the wearer to freely fly with an astral projection. They may choose to be invisible, may fly, etc, and can move up to 500 feet from their body. This item can only be used while dead."},{"n": "Thundercage","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small metal domed cage appears at first glance to be a bird cage with two small openable doors. When opened the cage will attempt to suck in a shrink the opener and pull them insde (Int Save DC 13). If no other creature is pulled inside within 1 minute they are expelled, returned to their normal size and are free to go. If multiple creatures are sucked inside they must fight until all but one party are dead or unconscious and cannot leave the cage for any reason."},{"n": "Bauble of Snap Traps","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This glass bauble has several sharp metal teeth sticking out of it in various directions. When broken it spawns 9 metal snap traps that immediately arm in the tile and every adjacent tile. When a creature steps into a tile with a trap they suffer 2d10 piercing damage as the trap triggers (Dexterity Save 11 to avoid)"},{"n": "Balloon of Limited Freedom","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This is a small red balloon with a metal wire and hook. When activated this balloon inflates and pulls up the creature it is attached to into the air at a rate fo 20 feet per round. A creature trying to escape from the balloon must make a Dexterity Check DC 15 to escape otherwise they are continued to be pulled into the air. The balloon never comes down and is ultimately lost when used. If the balloon is stopped by say a stone cieling, it will slowly tunnel through it at a rate of 5 ft per round."},{"n": "Gravity Cube","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small tungsten cube is made up of connected smaller cubes. When twisted around one round later the cube will be to vacuum all nearby objects inside. Each round after it is activated it will attempt to suck in each non-grounded object within 50 feet by moving them 10 feet closer to the Cube. Movement in the opposite direction costs twice as much. Tiny or smaller objects will get pulled inside the cube and may be retrieved later by the owner of the cube. This effect lasts for 1 minute and cannot be used again for 24 hours after activation."},{"n": "Orb of Mass Destruction","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This orb is tiny but radiates with magical enemy humming and feeling dangerous to the touch. It can rolled with the user an an action and preceeds their movement. If it collides with an object smaller than it (Diminutive to start). Once it consumes 4 objects it will increase in size. The size changes are Tiny > Small > Medium > Large > Huge > Garganutian and each time it increases in size the number of objects needed to increase in size doubles (so 4 / 8 / 16 / 32 / 64 for maximum size). Unwilling creatures can make a Con Save DC 8+2 per size or are sucked into the orb."},{"n": "Friendly Familiar","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This small pink owl will fly near the attuned user and never stray far from their side for long, even if asked. It can fly and will scout short distances for the user. Additionally, the user is treated as proficient in Perception checks and give them dark vision 30 feet. It will very politely compliment and be kind to the user as much as it can, and gently speak helpful and supportive advice. It also even seeks to gather compliments from others nearby to further support the user."},{"n": "Orangebeards Useful Keg","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This magic keg can be filled with most things. When shaken the keg will transmute it into a full keg of alchohalic beverage that tastes somewhat like the objects originally added."},{"n": "Radiant Sheath","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This sheath can be fitted to hold any melee weapon. When the weapon is sheathed for at least an hour when drawn it covers the weapon in the chosen element for a full minute. Adding +1d6 Elemental Damage"},{"n": "Swordbreaker Gauntlet","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "As a reaction - before an attack is rolled you can choose to get hit. If so you have the opponent's item must make a Strength save. DC 14 - or the weapon is broken. It can gain a bonus to this save based on the strength of material, and has advantage on this save if it's magical. A weapon that passes this save cannot be affected again for a full day."},{"n": "Spelleater Gloves","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "As a reaction can cast counterspell as a 3rd level spell. If successful gain Xd6 temporary health per spell level eaten and can be recast within an hour as if it were your own spell. The gauntlet cannot be used again for X days where X is the level of the spell absorbed."},{"n": "Conductors Gloves","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "With a command word your hands and forearms will be removed from your body painlessly. They can float, interact, and attack up to 10 feet away from your body, while flying they have an AC of 18. If they are attacked directly and hit return to your body and not used again until a short rest."},{"n": "Amulet of Deception","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "As a Reaction if you are hit by any attack or spell you may activate this. The amulet will creaste a copy of your body that will ragdoll back and appear dead, at the the same time you turn invisible, as the spell for up to 1 minute. An investigation or perception check DC 15."},{"n": "Coin of Immense Value","r": "","t": "Wondrous","u": "","d": "This Sentient platinum coin has the face of a smiling man carved into it. While held it grants +1 proficiency bonus to any bartering or negotiation that involves the trading or exchange of good (including stuff like Hostages, etc) by whispering a small suggestion telepathically to the holder. If the coin itself is part of the exchange or barter it grants the user advantage if, and only if they value the coin at over 500 gold pieces in value in which case the smile turns into a massive grin. Anything less than 500 gold pieces grants disadvantage on that same check (they retain the +1 though) and the coins face turns into an angry scowl."}];
